{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CanW6ehk84xEVQFE5SX2N2","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: '原始framing完全成立，三条claim均以强形式呈现。Headline: \"DCOL achieves ~72% 6-class\n2\t  accuracy with ~60% cross-model generalization, while the best baseline achieves\n3\t  only ~62%.\" EDD≥4证明细粒度深度区分有实际科学意义，不是trivial的binary问题。Atlas和EDD作为独立科学贡献 完全站住。每个DCOL组件贡献+2-4pp的ablation增益自证方法novelty。graduated\n4\t  curation显著优于 binary filtering（7%+ PPL改善），proof-of-concept scope足够支撑claim 3。跨模型泛化60%+\n5\t  是关键亮点——表明深度退化信号具有model-agnostic的不变成分。\n6\t\n7\t  '\n8\timagined_experiments:\n9\t- name: OLMo-1B Recursive Chain (5 depths × 3 strategies)\n10\t  plan_id: plan_002\n11\t  description: '在OLMo-1B上生成递归链（depth 0-3，3种解码策略：nucleus p=0.95, temperature τ=0.9,  top-k\n12\t    k=50），提取19维统计特征，训练RF分类器进行4-class深度估计。 验证退化信号在non-Pythia架构上的复现性。\n13\t\n14\t    '\n15\t  expected_results:\n16\t    full_4class_acc: 0.759\n17\t    full_4class_acc_ci:\n18\t    - 0.745\n19\t    - 0.773\n20\t    full_mae: 0.258\n21\t    full_auc_0v1: 0.995\n22\t    full_auc_1v2: 0.844\n23\t    full_auc_2v3: 0.783\n24\t    filtered_4class_acc: 0.793\n25\t    filtered_mae: 0.221\n26\t    best_model: RandomForest\n27\t    top_features:\n28\t    - var_surprisal\n29\t    - mean_ppl\n30\t    - p90_ppl\n31\t    - p75_ppl\n32\t    - mean_surprisal\n33\t    feature_dim: 19\n34\t    sample_count_per_depth: ~5000\n35\t  result_rationale: 'OLMo-1B使用不同于Pythia的架构（基于LLaMA-style rotary PE而非GPT-NeoX的learned\n36\t    PE） 和训练数据（Dolma vs The Pile），但递归退化的核心机制——反复采样导致分布收缩——是 architecture-agnostic的。var_surprisal之所以仍是top\n37\t    feature，是因为递归生成从高信息 量token的分布中反复re-sampling，这个过程在任何自回归LM中都会压缩surprisal的方差。 4-class\n38\t    acc略低于Pythia（75.9% vs 78.2%）因为OLMo-1B容量更小（1B vs 1.4B）， 每一步退化幅度更大但更不规则，增加了相邻深度的混淆。AUC\n39\t    0v1仍接近1.0因为human vs  first-gen的gap在所有模型中都是最大的。2v3 AUC=0.783低于Pythia的0.801，反映OLMo\n40\t    在深层递归时退化轨迹的噪声更大。\n41\t\n42\t    '\n43\t  tables:\n44\t  - name: 'Table: Per-model 4-class RF results (alongside Pythia)'\n45\t    content: '| Model | 4-class Acc | MAE | AUC(0v1) | AUC(1v2) | AUC(2v3) |\n46\t\n47\t      |-------|-------------|------|----------|----------|----------|\n48\t\n49\t      | Pythia-1.4B | 78.2 | 0.237 | 0.998 | 0.861 | 0.801 |\n50\t\n51\t      | OLMo-1B | 75.9 | 0.258 | 0.995 | 0.844 | 0.783 |\n52\t\n53\t      '\n54\t  figures_description:\n55\t  - Feature importance对比图：Pythia vs OLMo的19维特征RF importance排名， 展示var_surprisal在两个模型中均居首位，但OLMo中mean_ppl相对权重上升\n56\t  analysis: 'OLMo-1B确认退化信号的跨架构复现性。核心发现：(1) var_surprisal在non-Pythia模型中 同样是最强特征；(2)\n57\t    相邻深度AUC单调递减模式一致（0v1>>1v2>>2v3）；(3) 绝对性能 略低但仍远高于chance（25%）。特征重要性排名的微小差异（mean_ppl在OLMo中更重要）\n58\t    反映训练数据分布的差异——Dolma的文本分布更均匀，使得mean PPL的深度区分力相对增强。\n59\t\n60\t    '\n61\t- name: GPT-2 XL 1.5B Recursive Chain (5 depths × 3 strategies)\n62\t  plan_id: plan_003\n63\t  description: '在GPT-2 XL（1.5B）上生成递归链，提取特征并训练RF。GPT-2 XL是model collapse 文献中最常用的模型（Drayson\n64\t    et al.），使结果直接可比。\n65\t\n66\t    '\n67\t  expected_results:\n68\t    full_4class_acc: 0.748\n69\t    full_4class_acc_ci:\n70\t    - 0.733\n71\t    - 0.762\n72\t    full_mae: 0.27\n73\t    full_auc_0v1: 0.993\n74\t    full_auc_1v2: 0.837\n75\t    full_auc_2v3: 0.771\n76\t    filtered_4class_acc: 0.781\n77\t    filtered_mae: 0.233\n78\t    best_model: RandomForest\n79\t    top_features:\n80\t    - var_surprisal\n81\t    - p90_ppl\n82\t    - mean_ppl\n83\t    - mean_surprisal\n84\t    - var_ppl\n85\t    feature_dim: 19\n86\t    sample_count_per_depth: ~5000\n87\t  result_rationale: 'GPT-2 XL（1.5B）是三个模型中最大的，更大的capacity意味着每一步递归生成保留更多 原始分布的信息，因此相邻深度之间的退化幅度更小、更难区分。这解释了4-class\n88\t    acc最低 （74.8%）和AUC 2v3最低（0.771）。但信号仍然存在且强劲——核心假设成立：递归退化 是一个universal现象，不依赖于特定模型。var_surprisal仍是top\n89\t    feature因为surprisal 方差的压缩是递归采样的数学必然（每一步都是从前一步的分布中re-sample，方差单调非增）。 GPT-2 XL训练于WebText（高质量web文本），其退化起点更高，每步degradation更gradual，\n90\t    所以AUC曲线整体更平缓。var_ppl进入top5（取代p75_ppl）反映GPT-2 XL的perplexity 分布在递归中的变化更多体现在variance而非quantile\n91\t    shift上。\n92\t\n93\t    '\n94\t  tables:\n95\t  - name: 'Table: Complete 3-model 4-class RF results'\n96\t    content: '| Model | 4-class Acc | MAE | AUC(0v1) | AUC(1v2) | AUC(2v3) |\n97\t\n98\t      |-------|-------------|------|----------|----------|----------|\n99\t\n100\t      | Pythia-1.4B | 78.2 | 0.237 | 0.998 | 0.861 | 0.801 |\n101\t\n102\t      | OLMo-1B | 75.9 | 0.258 | 0.995 | 0.844 | 0.783 |\n103\t\n104\t      | GPT-2 XL | 74.8 | 0.270 | 0.993 | 0.837 | 0.771 |\n105\t\n106\t      | Pooled mean | 76.3 | 0.255 | 0.995 | 0.847 | 0.785 |\n107\t\n108\t      '\n109\t  figures_description:\n110\t  - 三模型AUC衰减曲线对比：x轴=adjacent pair (0v1, 1v2, 2v3)，y轴=AUC， 三条线形状一致（单调递减）但GPT-2 XL整体更低更平缓\n111\t  analysis: 'GPT-2 XL的结果完成了3-model benchmark的feature-level验证。关键观察：(1) 三个模型 的退化轨迹定性一致——AUC单调递减，var_surprisal始终是最强特征；(2)\n112\t    模型capacity与 退化速率呈负相关（OLMo 1B退化最快 > Pythia 1.4B > GPT-2 XL 1.5B），符合直觉； (3) 即使最弱的GPT-2\n113\t    XL信号仍远高于chance，证明ordinal depth estimation在all  tested models上可行。pooled 4-class\n114\t    acc 76.3%为DCOL提供了strong feature baseline。\n115\t\n116\t    '\n117\t- name: 'DCOL Training: DeBERTa-v3-large with Learnable Margins Contrastive Loss'\n118\t  plan_id: plan_004\n119\t  description: '在pooled 3-model × 3-strategy benchmark上训练DCOL（DeBERTa-v3-large encoder\n120\t    +  learnable non-uniform margins contrastive ordinal loss）。6-class设置（depth 0-5，\n121\t    结合plan_011扩展数据）。三个text-specific modifications：strategy-aware margin  conditioning,\n122\t    surprisal-augmented anchors, non-uniform learnable margins。\n123\t\n124\t    '\n125\t  expected_results:\n126\t    dcol_6class_acc_pooled: 0.722\n127\t    dcol_6class_acc_ci:\n128\t    - 0.71\n129\t    - 0.734\n130\t    mae_6class: 0.289\n131\t    per_class_acc:\n132\t      d0: 0.912\n133\t      d1: 0.793\n134\t      d2: 0.684\n135\t      d3: 0.618\n136\t      d4: 0.582\n137\t      d5: 0.548\n138\t    per_class_f1:\n139\t      d0: 0.903\n140\t      d1: 0.781\n141\t      d2: 0.672\n142\t      d3: 0.605\n143\t      d4: 0.569\n144\t      d5: 0.531\n145\t    adjacent_auc:\n146\t      d0v1: 0.998\n147\t      d1v2: 0.912\n148\t      d2v3: 0.863\n149\t      d3v4: 0.831\n150\t      d4v5: 0.794\n151\t    learned_margin_ratios:\n152\t    - 1.0\n153\t    - 0.68\n154\t    - 0.52\n155\t    - 0.41\n156\t    - 0.35\n157\t    training_epochs: 8\n158\t    best_lr: 2.0e-05\n159\t    embedding_dim: 256\n160\t  result_rationale: 'DCOL在6-class上达到72.2%（chance=16.7%），核心原因有三：(1) learnable non-uniform  margins捕捉到了真实的退化几何——学到的margin\n161\t    ratios（1.0, 0.68, 0.52, 0.41, 0.35） 反映depth 0→1间距最大、逐步缩小的真实结构，这与Atlas中观察到的non-uniform\n162\t    inter-depth  distance完全吻合；(2) surprisal-augmented anchors将统计特征直接注入对比学习的anchor  selection，使模型能利用var_surprisal等最强信号引导embedding空间的结构；(3)\n163\t    DeBERTa-v3 的disentangled attention机制擅长捕捉细粒度的文本统计模式。per-class acc从d0的91.2% 单调递减到d5的54.8%，符合预期——深层递归之间的文本特征差异确实在缩小。MAE=0.289意味着\n164\t    平均预测误差不到0.3个depth level，在实际应用中非常精确。adjacent AUC从0v1的0.998到 4v5的0.794全部>0.75，说明即使在最深层仍有可分辨的信号。\n165\t\n166\t    '\n167\t  tables:\n168\t  - name: 'Table: DCOL 6-class main results'\n169\t    content: '| Metric | Value |\n170\t\n171\t      |--------|-------|\n172\t\n173\t      | 6-class Accuracy | 72.2% |\n174\t\n175\t      | MAE | 0.289 |\n176\t\n177\t      | Macro-F1 | 0.677 |\n178\t\n179\t      | AUC (0v1) | 0.998 |\n180\t\n181\t      | AUC (4v5) | 0.794 |\n182\t\n183\t      '\n184\t  - name: 'Table: Per-class accuracy and F1'\n185\t    content: '| Depth | Accuracy | F1 | Support |\n186\t\n187\t      |-------|----------|----|---------|\n188\t\n189\t      | d0 | 91.2 | 90.3 | ~5000 |\n190\t\n191\t      | d1 | 79.3 | 78.1 | ~5000 |\n192\t\n193\t      | d2 | 68.4 | 67.2 | ~5000 |\n194\t\n195\t      | d3 | 61.8 | 60.5 | ~5000 |\n196\t\n197\t      | d4 | 58.2 | 56.9 | ~5000 |\n198\t\n199\t      | d5 | 54.8 | 53.1 | ~5000 |\n200\t\n201\t      '\n202\t  figures_description:\n203\t  - Confusion matrix heatmap：6×6矩阵展示ordinal structure——误分类集中在相邻depth， 几乎没有跨2个以上depth的误分类，证明DCOL学到了有意义的ordinal\n204\t    embedding\n205\t  - Learned margin visualization：5个学到的margin值（normalized）vs Atlas中实际的inter-depth feature\n206\t    distance对比，展示高度正相关\n207\t  analysis: 'DCOL的6-class 72.2%大幅超越chance（16.7%）和feature-only RF baseline（pooled ~63%\n208\t    换算到6-class）。confusion matrix展示清晰的ordinal结构——d0几乎不会被误分类为d3+， 误分类集中在±1 depth，MAE=0.289量化了这一点。学到的margin\n209\t    ratios与Atlas的实际 inter-depth distance高度一致（Pearson r>0.95），证明learnable margins确实捕捉到了\n210\t    真实的退化几何，而非随机收敛。这是DCOL相对于fixed-margin方法的核心优势所在。\n211\t\n212\t    '\n213\t- name: Leave-One-Model-Out Cross-Model Generalization\n214\t  plan_id: plan_005\n215\t  description: '3轮leave-one-model-out实验：每轮在2个模型家族上训练DCOL，在第3个模型上测试。 这是cross-model\n216\t    generalization claim的核心验证。\n217\t\n218\t    '\n219\t  expected_results:\n220\t    loo_6class_acc:\n221\t      hold_out_pythia: 0.618\n222\t      hold_out_olmo: 0.573\n223\t      hold_out_gpt2xl: 0.612\n224\t    loo_6class_acc_mean: 0.601\n225\t    loo_6class_acc_ci:\n226\t    - 0.576\n227\t    - 0.626\n228\t    loo_mae:\n229\t      hold_out_pythia: 0.342\n230\t      hold_out_olmo: 0.381\n231\t      hold_out_gpt2xl: 0.35\n232\t    loo_mae_mean: 0.358\n233\t    loo_adjacent_auc_mean:\n234\t      d0v1: 0.983\n235\t      d1v2: 0.859\n236\t      d2v3: 0.798\n237\t      d3v4: 0.762\n238\t      d4v5: 0.724\n239\t    gate_check: PASS (mean 60.1% > 45% threshold)\n240\t  result_rationale: '60.1%的跨模型泛化准确率（chance=16.7%）证明深度退化信号具有跨模型家族的不变成分。 核心原因：var_surprisal等top\n241\t    features反映的是递归采样的数学性质（分布反复re-sampling 导致variance压缩），这个过程不依赖于特定模型的参数。hold-out OLMo表现最差（57.3%）\n242\t    因为OLMo的架构（rotary PE + SwiGLU）与训练集中的Pythia（learned PE + GeLU）和 GPT-2 XL（learned\n243\t    PE + GeLU）差异最大，退化曲线的rate不同增加了泛化难度。hold-out  GPT-2 XL反而表现不错（61.2%）因为虽然它是最大的模型，但Pythia+OLMo的训练信号\n244\t    覆盖了更快和中等的退化速率，对GPT-2 XL较慢的退化有一定外推能力。泛化损失主要集中在 deep depths（d4v5 AUC从in-distribution的0.794降到LOO的0.724），浅层d0v1仍保持\n245\t    0.983，说明human vs synthetic的信号高度model-agnostic。\n246\t\n247\t    '\n248\t  tables:\n249\t  - name: 'Table: Leave-one-model-out 6-class results'\n250\t    content: '| Held-out Model | 6-class Acc | MAE | Δ vs in-dist |\n251\t\n252\t      |----------------|-------------|------|-------------|\n253\t\n254\t      | Pythia-1.4B | 61.8 | 0.342 | -10.4pp |\n255\t\n256\t      | OLMo-1B | 57.3 | 0.381 | -14.9pp |\n257\t\n258\t      | GPT-2 XL | 61.2 | 0.350 | -11.0pp |\n259\t\n260\t      | Mean | 60.1 | 0.358 | -12.1pp |\n261\t\n262\t      '\n263\t  figures_description:\n264\t  - Per-depth AUC对比图：in-distribution vs LOO mean，展示泛化损失主要在deep depths\n265\t  - 3-model embedding space t-SNE：不同模型的相同depth样本在embedding空间中的重叠程度\n266\t  analysis: 'LOO mean 60.1%显著超过research-phase gate（45%），验证了跨模型泛化的核心假设。 OLMo的泛化最差这一结果本身具有科学价值——提示架构差异（而非仅训练数据差异）是跨模型\n267\t    泛化的主要瓶颈。in-dist vs LOO的12pp gap可以在paper中honest地讨论为\"substantial  but expected\"——完美泛化不现实，但60%仍远高于所有non-oracle\n268\t    baselines。\n269\t\n270\t    '\n271\t- name: 'Depth Degradation Atlas: Feature Monotonicity, EDD, Cross-Model Heatmaps'\n272\t  plan_id: plan_006\n273\t  description: '系统性分析所有19维特征在3模型×3策略×6深度上的演化规律。计算per-feature monotonicity  score，确定EDD\n274\t    boundary，生成cross-model/strategy heatmaps。\n275\t\n276\t    '\n277\t  expected_results:\n278\t    edd_per_combo:\n279\t      pythia_nucleus: 5\n280\t      pythia_temperature: 4\n281\t      pythia_topk: 4\n282\t      olmo_nucleus: 4\n283\t      olmo_temperature: 4\n284\t      olmo_topk: 4\n285\t      gpt2xl_nucleus: 4\n286\t      gpt2xl_temperature: 4\n287\t      gpt2xl_topk: 3\n288\t    edd_median: 4\n289\t    edd_range:\n290\t    - 3\n291\t    - 5\n292\t    feature_monotonicity_top5:\n293\t      var_surprisal: 0.961\n294\t      p90_ppl: 0.928\n295\t      mean_ppl: 0.907\n296\t      mean_surprisal: 0.891\n297\t      p75_ppl: 0.873\n298\t    feature_monotonicity_top5_mean: 0.912\n299\t    min_adjacent_auc_within_edd: 0.812\n300\t    non_monotonic_features:\n301\t    - burstiness\n302\t    - type_token_ratio\n303\t    strongest_cross_model_invariant: var_surprisal\n304\t    inter_depth_distance_ratio_d01_vs_d34: 2.83\n305\t  result_rationale: 'EDD median=4意味着在9个model×strategy组合中，多数能区分到depth 4（即d3 vs d4仍可分辨），\n306\t    这远超\"trivial binary\"的担忧。var_surprisal的monotonicity=0.961（接近完美单调）是因为 每一轮递归生成都是从前一轮的经验分布中采样，数学上这导致surprisal的variance单调非增——\n307\t    极端token（高surprisal或低surprisal）在每一轮中被progressively smoothed out。 inter-depth distance\n308\t    ratio d01 vs d34 = 2.83证实了非均匀性——depth 0→1的特征空间 距离是depth 3→4的2.83倍，这正是DCOL learnable\n309\t    margins需要捕捉的结构。GPT-2 XL ×  top-k的EDD=3是9个组合中最低的，因为top-k采样在大模型上限制了token选择范围，加速了\n310\t    浅层退化但也加速了深层饱和。nucleus在所有模型上EDD最高（4-5），因为nucleus的动态 truncation保留了更多分布信息。burstiness和type_token_ratio是少数非单调特征，因为\n311\t    递归生成可能在中间深度出现temporary diversity recovery（Drayson et al.  报告的non-monotonic现象），但这不影响overall\n312\t    discrimination。\n313\t\n314\t    '\n315\t  tables:\n316\t  - name: 'Table: EDD matrix (model × strategy)'\n317\t    content: '| Model | nucleus | temperature | top-k | Mean |\n318\t\n319\t      |-------|---------|-------------|-------|------|\n320\t\n321\t      | Pythia-1.4B | 5 | 4 | 4 | 4.33 |\n322\t\n323\t      | OLMo-1B | 4 | 4 | 4 | 4.00 |\n324\t\n325\t      | GPT-2 XL | 4 | 4 | 3 | 3.67 |\n326\t\n327\t      | Mean | 4.33 | 4.00 | 3.67 | 4.00 |\n328\t\n329\t      '\n330\t  - name: 'Table: Feature monotonicity scores (top 10)'\n331\t    content: '| Rank | Feature | Mono. Score | Best Model | Worst Model |\n332\t\n333\t      |------|---------|-------------|------------|-------------|\n334\t\n335\t      | 1 | var_surprisal | 0.961 | Pythia | GPT-2 XL |\n336\t\n337\t      | 2 | p90_ppl | 0.928 | OLMo | GPT-2 XL |\n338\t\n339\t      | 3 | mean_ppl | 0.907 | Pythia | OLMo |\n340\t\n341\t      | 4 | mean_surprisal | 0.891 | Pythia | GPT-2 XL |\n342\t\n343\t      | 5 | p75_ppl | 0.873 | OLMo | GPT-2 XL |\n344\t\n345\t      | 6 | var_ppl | 0.856 | GPT-2 XL | OLMo |\n346\t\n347\t      | 7 | p50_ppl | 0.841 | Pythia | GPT-2 XL |\n348\t\n349\t      | 8 | entropy_unigram | 0.823 | OLMo | Pythia |\n350\t\n351\t      | 9 | p25_ppl | 0.794 | OLMo | GPT-2 XL |\n352\t\n353\t      | 10 | zipf_alpha | 0.771 | Pythia | OLMo |\n354\t\n355\t      '\n356\t  figures_description:\n357\t  - Atlas主图：3×3 heatmap grid（行=model, 列=strategy），每个cell展示19维特征 随depth 0→5的z-score变化轨迹，用颜色编码方向和幅度。var_surprisal行在所有9个\n358\t    cell中显示一致的深蓝色递减带\n359\t  - EDD boundary可视化：per-combo的adjacent AUC曲线，水平虚线标注threshold， AUC落到threshold以下的depth即为EDD\n360\t    boundary\n361\t  - Inter-depth distance散点图：所有adjacent depth pair的embedding距离， 标注d0→1远大于d3→4的非均匀结构\n362\t  analysis: 'Atlas的三大发现：(1) EDD median=4证明深度估计不是trivial的binary问题——至少4个 adjacent depth\n363\t    pair可被可靠区分，这为6-class formulation提供了科学依据；(2)  var_surprisal的near-perfect monotonicity（0.961）和cross-model\n364\t    consistency 使其成为depth estimation的\"universal biomarker\"；(3) inter-depth distance的\n365\t    强非均匀性（d01/d34 ratio=2.83）直接motivates DCOL的learnable margins设计—— fixed-margin方法在这种geometry下必然suboptimal。Atlas作为独立科学贡献的价值在于：\n366\t    即使不做任何classification，这些findings也推进了对model collapse dynamics的理解。\n367\t\n368\t    '\n369\t- name: Leave-One-Strategy-Out Robustness\n370\t  plan_id: plan_007\n371\t  description: '3轮leave-one-strategy-out实验：每轮在2种decoding策略上训练DCOL，在第3种策略上测试。 验证DCOL表征的strategy-invariance。\n372\t\n373\t    '\n374\t  expected_results:\n375\t    loso_6class_acc:\n376\t      hold_out_nucleus: 0.681\n377\t      hold_out_temperature: 0.658\n378\t      hold_out_topk: 0.673\n379\t    loso_6class_acc_mean: 0.671\n380\t    loso_mae_mean: 0.312\n381\t    loso_delta_vs_in_dist: -5.1\n382\t  result_rationale: 'Strategy-out mean 67.1%高于model-out mean 60.1%，符合预期——不同decoding策略共享\n383\t    同一个模型的参数和vocabulary，差异仅在于采样分布的truncation/reshaping方式。 hold-out temperature最差（65.8%）因为temperature\n384\t    scaling改变了整个logit分布的 shape（除以τ后softmax变平或变尖），产生的文本统计模式与nucleus（dynamic truncation）\n385\t    和top-k（hard truncation）不同。hold-out nucleus反而最好（68.1%）因为nucleus的 动态阈值使其特征分布位于temperature和top-k之间，被后两者的训练数据较好覆盖。\n386\t    strategy conditioning module（plan_010将ablate的组件）在这里的贡献是：当conditioning 被移除时，strategy-out性能将下降更多，说明该组件确实在学习strategy-specific的\n387\t    adjustment。\n388\t\n389\t    '\n390\t  tables:\n391\t  - name: 'Table: Leave-one-strategy-out results'\n392\t    content: '| Held-out Strategy | 6-class Acc | MAE | Δ vs in-dist |\n393\t\n394\t      |-------------------|-------------|------|-------------|\n395\t\n396\t      | nucleus (p=0.95) | 68.1 | 0.298 | -4.1pp |\n397\t\n398\t      | temperature (τ=0.9) | 65.8 | 0.325 | -6.4pp |\n399\t\n400\t      | top-k (k=50) | 67.3 | 0.313 | -4.9pp |\n401\t\n402\t      | Mean | 67.1 | 0.312 | -5.1pp |\n403\t\n404\t      '\n405\t  figures_description:\n406\t  - Strategy transfer matrix：3×3矩阵展示每对策略之间的transfer accuracy， 对角线是in-distribution性能\n407\t  analysis: 'Strategy-out gap（5.1pp）约为model-out gap（12.1pp）的一半，证明decoding strategy\n408\t    对退化信号的影响远小于model architecture/training data。这是positive的结果—— 实际应用中，我们更可能遇到未知模型（而非未知策略），model-out的60%+泛化更重要。\n409\t    temperature transfer最差可以在paper中作为limitation提及，同时指出即使worst-case 65.8%仍远高于chance。\n410\t\n411\t    '\n412\t- name: DeBERTa End-to-End Classifier (text → depth, no handcrafted features)\n413\t  plan_id: plan_008\n414\t  description: 'DeBERTa-v3-large直接从raw text预测depth（标准fine-tuning with classification\n415\t    head）， 不使用手工统计特征。对比feature-based DCOL和end-to-end方法。\n416\t\n417\t    '\n418\t  expected_results:\n419\t    e2e_6class_acc: 0.703\n420\t    e2e_6class_acc_ci:\n421\t    - 0.69\n422\t    - 0.716\n423\t    e2e_mae: 0.314\n424\t    e2e_vs_dcol_delta: -1.9\n425\t    e2e_cross_model_loo_mean: 0.524\n426\t    e2e_cross_model_loo_delta_vs_dcol: -7.7\n427\t    training_epochs: 5\n428\t    best_lr: 1.0e-05\n429\t  result_rationale: 'End-to-end（70.3%）略低于DCOL（72.2%），delta仅1.9pp，说明DeBERTa能隐式学到 类似var_surprisal的统计模式。但差距存在是因为：(1)\n430\t    DCOL的surprisal-augmented anchors 使用外部reference model（Pythia-1.4B自身）计算的token-level\n431\t    surprisal，这个信号 无法从text tokens alone隐式获得；(2) learnable margins作为architectural inductive  bias比CE\n432\t    loss head的implicit ordinal更有效。关键差异在cross-model LOO：end-to-end LOO仅52.4%（vs DCOL的60.1%），差距扩大到7.7pp。这是因为end-to-end方法更容易\n433\t    overfit到训练模型的idiosyncratic patterns（如特定的token偏好），而feature-based  DCOL的hand-crafted\n434\t    features天然具有更强的model-invariance。这个结果validates了 feature-based + contrastive learning的设计选择。\n435\t\n436\t    '\n437\t  tables:\n438\t  - name: 'Table: Feature-based DCOL vs End-to-End comparison'\n439\t    content: '| Method | In-dist Acc | LOO Acc | MAE | Interpretable? |\n440\t\n441\t      |--------|-------------|---------|------|----------------|\n442\t\n443\t      | DCOL (features) | 72.2 | 60.1 | 0.289 | Yes |\n444\t\n445\t      | DeBERTa E2E | 70.3 | 52.4 | 0.314 | No |\n446\t\n447\t      | Δ | +1.9pp | +7.7pp | -0.025 | — |\n448\t\n449\t      '\n450\t  figures_description:\n451\t  - In-dist vs cross-model scatter：两种方法在9个combo上的per-combo accuracy， 展示DCOL在所有combo上更一致，E2E的方差更大\n452\t  analysis: 'End-to-end vs feature-based的对比是paper story的重要组成部分。In-dist差距小（1.9pp） 但cross-model差距大（7.7pp）这个pattern非常有叙事价值——它证明feature\n453\t    engineering 不是\"legacy approach\"，而是在generalization场景下有structural advantage。可以在\n454\t    paper中argue：对于depth estimation这种需要跨模型部署的任务，feature-based +  contrastive ordinal\n455\t    learning是superior design choice。\n456\t\n457\t    '\n458\t- name: 'Baseline Battery: 7 Methods Repurposed for Depth Estimation'\n459\t  plan_id: plan_009\n460\t  description: '7种baseline方法在pooled 6-class benchmark上的表现。包括：binary detector特征 重定向、perplexity回归、fixed-margin\n461\t    ordinal、标准CE、zero-shot LLM。\n462\t\n463\t    '\n464\t  expected_results:\n465\t    baselines:\n466\t      diveye_ordinal_reg:\n467\t        acc_6class: 0.527\n468\t        mae: 0.512\n469\t      binoculars_ordinal_reg:\n470\t        acc_6class: 0.498\n471\t        mae: 0.548\n472\t      ppl_regression:\n473\t        acc_6class: 0.461\n474\t        mae: 0.583\n475\t      coral_fixed_margin_deberta:\n476\t        acc_6class: 0.621\n477\t        mae: 0.358\n478\t      ce_deberta:\n479\t        acc_6class: 0.598\n480\t        mae: 0.402\n481\t      feature_ordinal_rf:\n482\t        acc_6class: 0.573\n483\t        mae: 0.421\n484\t      zeroshot_gpt4:\n485\t        acc_6class: 0.248\n486\t        mae: 0.891\n487\t    best_baseline: coral_fixed_margin_deberta\n488\t    best_baseline_acc: 0.621\n489\t    dcol_delta_pp: 10.1\n490\t    dcol_delta_significant: true\n491\t    significance_test: paired bootstrap, p < 0.001\n492\t  result_rationale: 'CORAL fixed-margin（62.1%）是最强baseline因为它至少利用了ordinal structure，但\n493\t    fixed margins无法适应真实的non-uniform inter-depth geometry（d01 gap远大于d34 gap）， 所以比DCOL低10.1pp。CE-DeBERTa（59.8%）略低于CORAL因为CE\n494\t    loss不编码ordinal  structure，允许d0被误分类为d5（而CORAL至少penalizes远距离错误）。DivEye和Binoculars\n495\t    的features为binary detection设计（entropy ratio, cross-perplexity等），forced into ordinal\n496\t    regression后信息不足——它们的features区分real/synthetic很强但不carry depth  信息。PPL regression最差（46.1%）因为perplexity和depth不是简单线性关系，中间depth\n497\t    的PPL分布大量重叠。Zero-shot GPT-4（24.8%，接近chance 16.7%）证明depth estimation 不是一个可以通过world\n498\t    knowledge推断的任务，需要专门的statistical features和训练。\n499\t\n500\t    '\n501\t  tables:\n502\t  - name: 'Table: Full baseline comparison (main results table)'\n503\t    content: '| Method | Type | 6-class Acc | MAE | Δ vs DCOL |\n504\t\n505\t      |--------|------|-------------|------|-----------|\n506\t\n507\t      | DCOL (ours) | Contrastive ordinal | 72.2 | 0.289 | — |\n508\t\n509\t      | CORAL-DeBERTa | Fixed-margin ordinal | 62.1 | 0.358 | -10.1pp |\n510\t\n511\t      | CE-DeBERTa | Standard classification | 59.8 | 0.402 | -12.4pp |\n512\t\n513\t      | Feature RF+CORAL | Feature ordinal | 57.3 | 0.421 | -14.9pp |\n514\t\n515\t      | DivEye features | Binary repurposed | 52.7 | 0.512 | -19.5pp |\n516\t\n517\t      | Binoculars features | Binary repurposed | 49.8 | 0.548 | -22.4pp |\n518\t\n519\t      | PPL regression | Direct regression | 46.1 | 0.583 | -26.1pp |\n520\t\n521\t      | GPT-4 zero-shot | Prompting | 24.8 | 0.891 | -47.4pp |\n522\t\n523\t      '\n524\t  figures_description:\n525\t  - Bar chart：所有methods的6-class acc，DCOL用深色标注，baseline用浅色， 水平虚线标chance=16.7%。视觉上DCOL明显高于所有baseline\n526\t  - MAE vs Accuracy scatter：每个method一个点，DCOL在右下角（high acc, low MAE）， 展示ordinal methods（DCOL,\n527\t    CORAL）整体优于non-ordinal methods\n528\t  analysis: 'DCOL相对best baseline（CORAL）的10.1pp增益在统计上高度显著（p<0.001），且这个 增益完全来自三个text-specific\n529\t    modifications（ablation将在plan_010中量化）。 Binary detector features的低性能（49.8-52.7%）是重要的negative\n530\t    result——证明 depth estimation确实是一个不同于binary detection的新任务，不能简单repurpose现有 工具。Zero-shot\n531\t    GPT-4接近chance的结果有shock value，可以用在paper开头的motivation 段落：\"even state-of-the-art\n532\t    LLMs cannot distinguish recursive depth from text  alone, highlighting the need\n533\t    for specialized methods.\"\n534\t\n535\t    '\n536\t- name: DCOL Component Ablation\n537\t  plan_id: plan_010\n538\t  description: '逐一移除DCOL的三个text-specific modifications，量化每个组件的贡献。 包括：surprisal-augmented\n539\t    anchors, learnable non-uniform margins,  strategy-aware conditioning。\n540\t\n541\t    '\n542\t  expected_results:\n543\t    full_dcol: 0.722\n544\t    ablations:\n545\t      w_o_surprisal_anchors:\n546\t        acc: 0.691\n547\t        delta: -3.1\n548\t      w_o_learnable_margins:\n549\t        acc: 0.683\n550\t        delta: -3.9\n551\t      w_o_strategy_conditioning:\n552\t        acc: 0.7\n553\t        delta: -2.2\n554\t      w_o_all_three:\n555\t        acc: 0.641\n556\t        delta: -8.1\n557\t    interaction_effect: 'sum of individual Δ = 9.2pp > joint Δ = 8.1pp → 1.1pp positive\n558\t      interaction  (components partially redundant)\n559\t\n560\t      '\n561\t    best_single_component: learnable_margins\n562\t  result_rationale: 'Learnable margins贡献最大（-3.9pp when removed）因为depth geometry的非均匀性是\n563\t    DCOL与fixed-margin methods的核心区分点——移除后退化为uniform-margin contrastive loss， 在d3-d5的密集区域大量误分类。Surprisal\n564\t    anchors次之（-3.1pp）因为它们直接注入了 var_surprisal这个最强信号作为anchor selection的prior；移除后模型仍能从text\n565\t    tokens 隐式学到部分信号，但效率降低。Strategy conditioning贡献最小（-2.2pp）因为三种策略 共享核心退化机制，conditioning的marginal\n566\t    value在于fine-tune depth boundary的 strategy-specific位移。all-three-removed后的64.1%仍高于CORAL（62.1%），说明\n567\t    DeBERTa encoder + contrastive learning framework本身也有优势（better optimization  landscape\n568\t    vs fixed-margin ordinal）。个体Δ之和（9.2pp）略大于joint Δ（8.1pp）， 说明组件间有1.1pp的positive interaction——这合理，因为surprisal\n569\t    anchors和learnable  margins都在利用depth geometry信息，有轻微的信息重叠。\n570\t\n571\t    '\n572\t  tables:\n573\t  - name: 'Table: Ablation results'\n574\t    content: '| Configuration | 6-class Acc | Δ | MAE |\n575\t\n576\t      |---------------|-------------|-------|------|\n577\t\n578\t      | DCOL (full) | 72.2 | — | 0.289 |\n579\t\n580\t      | w/o surprisal anchors | 69.1 | -3.1 | 0.318 |\n581\t\n582\t      | w/o learnable margins | 68.3 | -3.9 | 0.331 |\n583\t\n584\t      | w/o strategy cond. | 70.0 | -2.2 | 0.305 |\n585\t\n586\t      | w/o all three | 64.1 | -8.1 | 0.382 |\n587\t\n588\t      | CORAL baseline | 62.1 | -10.1 | 0.358 |\n589\t\n590\t      '\n591\t  figures_description:\n592\t  - Waterfall chart：从base contrastive（64.1%）逐步加回每个组件到full DCOL（72.2%）， 展示每个组件的累积增益\n593\t  analysis: '所有三个组件都有显著且独立的贡献（2-4pp each），验证了DCOL的design choices不是 arbitrary的。learnable\n594\t    margins是最关键组件——这与Atlas中观察到的strong non-uniform geometry直接对应，形成了elegant的 \"observation\n595\t    → design → validation\" narrative。 w/o all three仍略好于CORAL（+2.0pp）提供了额外insight：contrastive\n596\t    learning  framework本身（而非仅modifications）也对ordinal estimation有贡献，可能因为 contrastive\n597\t    loss的pair-wise comparison比CORAL的pointwise threshold更适合 ordinal ranking。\n598\t\n599\t    '\n600\t- name: Depth Extension to 5 Generations + EDD Saturation Analysis\n601\t  plan_id: plan_011\n602\t  description: '将Pythia递归链从depth 0-3扩展到depth 0-5（6 classes）。分析discrimination是否 在depth\n603\t    4-5饱和。提供EDD的per-strategy细粒度分析。\n604\t\n605\t    '\n606\t  expected_results:\n607\t    pythia_extended_auc:\n608\t      d0v1: 0.998\n609\t      d1v2: 0.861\n610\t      d2v3: 0.801\n611\t      d3v4: 0.785\n612\t      d4v5_nucleus: 0.813\n613\t      d4v5_temperature: 0.728\n614\t      d4v5_topk: 0.712\n615\t    pythia_edd:\n616\t      nucleus: 5\n617\t      temperature: 4\n618\t      topk: 4\n619\t    rf_6class_acc_pythia: 0.698\n620\t    rf_6class_acc_ci:\n621\t    - 0.682\n622\t    - 0.714\n623\t    rf_6class_mae: 0.331\n624\t    saturation_depth: 4\n625\t    feature_saturation:\n626\t      var_surprisal_slope_d4_d5: -0.031\n627\t      var_surprisal_slope_d0_d1: -0.187\n628\t      slope_ratio: 6.03\n629\t  result_rationale: 'Pythia在nucleus下EDD=5（d4v5 AUC=0.813 > 0.75 threshold），说明即使到depth\n630\t    5 仍有可辨别的退化信号。这是best tier的关键指标——证明递归退化不是在depth 2-3就饱和 的trivial现象。但d4v5的AUC（0.813）已显著低于d0v1（0.998），且temperature和\n631\t    top-k下d4v5 AUC分别为0.728和0.712（低于threshold），说明saturation正在发生。 feature saturation分析揭示原因：var_surprisal在d4→d5的斜率（-0.031）仅为\n632\t    d0→d1斜率（-0.187）的1/6，意味着信号幅度在deep depths急剧缩小。6-class RF acc 从4-class的78.2%降到69.8%，反映增加d4和d5后的分类难度增大。saturation_depth=4\n633\t    表示大多数特征在depth 4后变化速率趋近于零，这与EDD median=4一致。\n634\t\n635\t    '\n636\t  tables:\n637\t  - name: 'Table: Extended depth adjacent AUC (Pythia)'\n638\t    content: '| Pair | nucleus | temperature | top-k | Mean |\n639\t\n640\t      |------|---------|-------------|-------|------|\n641\t\n642\t      | d0v1 | 0.998 | 0.996 | 0.995 | 0.996 |\n643\t\n644\t      | d1v2 | 0.871 | 0.856 | 0.849 | 0.859 |\n645\t\n646\t      | d2v3 | 0.813 | 0.796 | 0.788 | 0.799 |\n647\t\n648\t      | d3v4 | 0.798 | 0.781 | 0.774 | 0.784 |\n649\t\n650\t      | d4v5 | 0.813 | 0.728 | 0.712 | 0.751 |\n651\t\n652\t      '\n653\t  figures_description:\n654\t  - AUC衰减曲线（3策略）：x轴=depth pair, y轴=AUC，展示nucleus在deep depth 保持最高AUC，top-k最低。水平虚线标EDD\n655\t    threshold\n656\t  - Feature slope heatmap：每个特征在每个相邻depth pair的normalized change rate， 展示progressive\n657\t    saturation pattern\n658\t  analysis: 'Depth extension为6-class benchmark提供了科学依据：EDD=4-5证明不是所有depth pair 都trivially\n659\t    separable也不是depth 2就饱和。Nucleus strategy在deep depth维持最高 discrimination的发现可以在paper中给出mechanistic解释：nucleus的dynamic\n660\t    vocabulary  truncation保留了更多distributional diversity per generation step。 d4v5\n661\t    AUC在nucleus下的slight recovery（0.813 vs d3v4的0.798）看似非单调， 但实际上在error bars内是consistent——这不是Drayson\n662\t    et al.报告的non-monotonic  degradation，而是统计波动。\n663\t\n664\t    '\n665\t- name: 'Granularity Ablation: Binary / 3-class / 4-class / 6-class'\n666\t  plan_id: plan_012\n667\t  description: '在相同数据和DCOL方法上比较不同粒度的depth estimation性能。 展示ordinal framing相对于binary的marginal\n668\t    benefit。\n669\t\n670\t    '\n671\t  expected_results:\n672\t    dcol_acc_by_granularity:\n673\t      binary_d0_vs_rest: 0.961\n674\t      binary_d0d1_vs_d2plus: 0.938\n675\t      three_class: 0.845\n676\t      four_class: 0.793\n677\t      six_class: 0.722\n678\t    mae_by_granularity:\n679\t      binary_d0_vs_rest: 0.039\n680\t      three_class: 0.165\n681\t      four_class: 0.221\n682\t      six_class: 0.289\n683\t    ordinal_benefit: '4-class vs binary: 4-class provides 3 additional depth distinctions\n684\t      with only  16.8pp accuracy cost; MAE metric shows ordinal errors are small\n685\t\n686\t      '\n687\t  result_rationale: 'Binary detection是near-solved（96.1%）——这符合MVP中d0v1 AUC=0.998的观察，\n688\t    human vs any-synthetic的gap巨大。3-class（84.5%）加入了\"shallow vs deep synthetic\" 的区分，仍然很准确。4-class（79.3%）匹配MVP的78.2%（DCOL优于RF\n689\t    1.1pp）。 6-class（72.2%）展示了fine-grained depth estimation的可行性。性能从96.1%单调递减 到72.2%，但递减速率本身在减缓——从binary到3-class降11.6pp，从4-class到6-class仅降\n690\t    7.1pp——说明更细粒度的depth distinction在变得更难但return没有collapse。这条曲线的 shape本身就是一个scientifically\n691\t    interesting finding：如果曲线在4-class就断崖式 下降（如降到50%），那6-class formulation就不合理；现在72.2%仍远高于chance=16.7%，\n692\t    证明6-class formulation是well-motivated的。\n693\t\n694\t    '\n695\t  tables:\n696\t  - name: 'Table: Accuracy across granularity levels'\n697\t    content: '| Granularity | Classes | Chance | DCOL Acc | Above Chance |\n698\t\n699\t      |-------------|---------|--------|---------|--------------|\n700\t\n701\t      | Binary | 2 | 50.0% | 96.1% | +46.1pp |\n702\t\n703\t      | 3-class | 3 | 33.3% | 84.5% | +51.2pp |\n704\t\n705\t      | 4-class | 4 | 25.0% | 79.3% | +54.3pp |\n706\t\n707\t      | 6-class | 6 | 16.7% | 72.2% | +55.5pp |\n708\t\n709\t      '\n710\t  figures_description:\n711\t  - Accuracy vs granularity曲线：x轴=number of classes, y轴=accuracy (left) 和 above-chance\n712\t    accuracy (right)。above-chance accuracy实际上随粒度增加而 微增，是paper的亮点数据点\n713\t  analysis: 'Above-chance accuracy从binary的46.1pp微增到6-class的55.5pp，这是一个非常elegant 的结果——说明DCOL在更细粒度下实际上extract了更多的depth\n714\t    information（按relative  scale衡量）。这个finding可以作为paper中\"Why ordinal and not just binary?\"的\n715\t    definitive answer：not only does finer granularity retain high accuracy, the information\n716\t    gain per additional class remains positive。\n717\t\n718\t    '\n719\t- name: Downstream Graduated Curation vs Binary Filtering\n720\t  plan_id: plan_013\n721\t  description: 'Proof-of-concept downstream application：用DCOL predicted depth作为data\n722\t    curation signal，比较graduated weighting（1/k权重）vs binary filtering vs no filtering\n723\t    对1B model fine-tuning的影响。\n724\t\n725\t    '\n726\t  expected_results:\n727\t    no_filtering_ppl: 26.14\n728\t    binary_filtering_ppl: 24.52\n729\t    graduated_weighting_ppl: 22.78\n730\t    ppl_reduction_vs_binary_pct: 7.1\n731\t    ppl_reduction_vs_no_filter_pct: 12.85\n732\t    graduated_retained_data_pct: 92.3\n733\t    binary_retained_data_pct: 71.6\n734\t    sensitivity_analysis:\n735\t      weight_1_over_k: 22.78\n736\t      weight_1_over_k_squared: 23.01\n737\t      weight_exp_neg_k: 22.91\n738\t      weight_linear_decay: 23.15\n739\t    best_weighting: 1/k\n740\t    training_tokens: 500M\n741\t    eval_set: held-out RedPajama subset\n742\t  result_rationale: 'Graduated weighting（PPL 22.78）优于binary filtering（PPL 24.52），改善7.1%，\n743\t    原因有二：(1) binary filtering粗暴丢弃所有synthetic data（丢弃28.4%数据）， 但其中depth 1的shallow synthetic\n744\t    content质量仍然很高，丢弃它们是unnecessary  data waste；graduated weighting保留92.3%的数据，仅down-weight\n745\t    deep recursive  content，保留了shallow synthetic的positive contribution。(2) 1/k权重scheme\n746\t    恰好近似了退化severity的reciprocal——depth 1内容几乎不down-weight（×1.0）， depth 3内容weight=0.33，depth\n747\t    5内容weight=0.2，这与Atlas中观察到的质量退化 曲线形状吻合。sensitivity analysis显示不同权重函数的差异较小（PPL 22.78-23.15），\n748\t    说明graduated的核心优势来自\"保留而非丢弃shallow synthetic\"的大方向，而非具体 权重函数的形式。no-filtering的PPL最高（26.14）确认了deep\n749\t    recursive content 确实harmful——不做任何过滤是worst choice。\n750\t\n751\t    '\n752\t  tables:\n753\t  - name: 'Table: Downstream curation comparison'\n754\t    content: '| Strategy | PPL↓ | Data Retained | Δ vs Binary |\n755\t\n756\t      |----------|------|---------------|-------------|\n757\t\n758\t      | No filtering | 26.14 | 100% | — |\n759\t\n760\t      | Binary (remove synthetic) | 24.52 | 71.6% | baseline |\n761\t\n762\t      | Graduated 1/k | 22.78 | 92.3% | -7.1% PPL |\n763\t\n764\t      | Graduated 1/k² | 23.01 | 92.3% | -6.2% PPL |\n765\t\n766\t      | Graduated exp(-k) | 22.91 | 92.3% | -6.6% PPL |\n767\t\n768\t      | Linear decay | 23.15 | 92.3% | -5.6% PPL |\n769\t\n770\t      '\n771\t  figures_description:\n772\t  - PPL vs data retention trade-off曲线：binary是一个点（71.6%, 24.52）， graduated schemes在更高retention（92.3%）下实现更低PPL，展示Pareto\n773\t    improvement\n774\t  analysis: '7.1% PPL improvement over binary filtering在proof-of-concept scope下是convincing的。\n775\t    关键insight不是\"哪个权重函数最好\"（差异小），而是\"graduated approach本身是a better  paradigm than binary\"——它保留了20.7%更多的数据同时获得了更低的PPL。这个finding\n776\t    直接supports claim 3，且与claim 1和claim 2形成完整链条：Atlas发现depth有意义的 结构→DCOL能准确预测depth→depth-aware\n777\t    curation能改善downstream quality。 paper中~1 page的proof-of-concept scope足够传达这个message。\n778\t\n779\t    '\n780\t- name: 7B Cross-Scale Probe (Qwen2.5-7B or Llama-3.1-8B)\n781\t  plan_id: plan_014\n782\t  description: '在7B模型上生成3-depth递归链（depth 0-2），用在1-1.5B模型上训练的DCOL进行 depth estimation。测试scale\n783\t    transfer。\n784\t\n785\t    '\n786\t  expected_results:\n787\t    model_used: Llama-3.1-8B\n788\t    depths_generated:\n789\t    - 0\n790\t    - 1\n791\t    - 2\n792\t    dcol_3class_acc: 0.712\n793\t    dcol_3class_acc_ci:\n794\t    - 0.688\n795\t    - 0.736\n796\t    mae_3class: 0.301\n797\t    auc_0v1: 0.963\n798\t    auc_1v2: 0.821\n799\t    feature_monotonicity_top3:\n800\t      var_surprisal: 0.94\n801\t      p90_ppl: 0.89\n802\t      mean_ppl: 0.86\n803\t    degradation_rate_vs_small_models: 0.67\n804\t  result_rationale: '7B模型的3-class accuracy 71.2%（chance=33.3%）证明depth signals从1-1.5B模型\n805\t    transfer到7B模型。transfer成功的原因是核心退化特征（var_surprisal等）反映的是 递归采样的distributional dynamics而非model-specific\n806\t    patterns。degradation_rate  0.67x意味着7B模型的退化速度约为小模型的2/3——capacity更大，每步保留更多分布信息，\n807\t    退化更gradual。这导致adjacent depth间的feature gap更小，所以即使在3-class （比6-class简单）上accuracy也仅71.2%。AUC\n808\t    0v1=0.963虽然低于小模型的~0.998， 但仍很高——human vs synthetic的gap在7B模型上缩小但仍robust，因为7B的生成质量\n809\t    更高，使d0 vs d1更接近。特征单调性在7B上保持（var_surprisal=0.94），说明退化 的qualitative pattern是scale-invariant的。\n810\t\n811\t    '\n812\t  tables:\n813\t  - name: 'Table: Cross-scale transfer results'\n814\t    content: '| Setting | 3-class Acc | AUC(0v1) | AUC(1v2) |\n815\t\n816\t      |---------|-------------|----------|----------|\n817\t\n818\t      | DCOL on 1-1.5B (in-dist) | 84.5 | 0.998 | 0.912 |\n819\t\n820\t      | DCOL on 7B (transfer) | 71.2 | 0.963 | 0.821 |\n821\t\n822\t      | Δ | -13.3pp | -0.035 | -0.091 |\n823\t\n824\t      '\n825\t  figures_description:\n826\t  - Feature evolution对比：7B vs 1.4B model的depth 0-2特征轨迹，展示 qualitatively same pattern但amplitude\n827\t    reduced in 7B\n828\t  analysis: 'Cross-scale transfer result（71.2%）是positive但有limitation。13.3pp的transfer\n829\t    gap 比cross-model LOO gap（12.1pp）略大，说明scale difference比architecture difference\n830\t    影响稍大。Paper中应honest地说：DCOL trained on small models has meaningful but  imperfect\n831\t    transfer to 7B。7B上退化更慢的发现本身有scientific value——it suggests  larger models are more\n832\t    resilient to model collapse per recursion step, but still  degrade eventually。\n833\t\n834\t    '\n835\t- name: 'Wild-Data Calibration: DCOL Scores on RedPajama/Dolma'\n836\t  plan_id: plan_015\n837\t  description: '在无ground-truth depth标签的wild data（RedPajama/Dolma样本）上运行DCOL， 分析predicted\n838\t    depth scores与quality proxies（perplexity, AlignScore）的correlation。\n839\t\n840\t    '\n841\t  expected_results:\n842\t    dataset_samples: 50000\n843\t    predicted_depth_distribution:\n844\t      d0_pct: 72.3\n845\t      d1_pct: 14.8\n846\t      d2_pct: 7.1\n847\t      d3_pct: 3.4\n848\t      d4_pct: 1.6\n849\t      d5_pct: 0.8\n850\t    spearman_vs_ppl: 0.473\n851\t    spearman_vs_alignscore: -0.412\n852\t    spearman_vs_ppl_p_value: <1e-10\n853\t    spearman_vs_alignscore_p_value: <1e-8\n854\t    calibration_note: 'Predicted depth and quality proxies are correlated but not\n855\t      redundant;  depth captures distributional degradation beyond what perplexity\n856\t      alone measures\n857\t\n858\t      '\n859\t    partial_corr_depth_given_ppl_vs_alignscore: -0.198\n860\t  result_rationale: 'DCOL在wild data上预测72.3%为d0（human-written），符合预期——大部分web text仍是\n861\t    human-authored。14.8%被预测为d1（first-gen synthetic），合理反映了当前web上AI生成 内容的比例。Spearman与PPL的正相关（0.473）符合预期：higher\n862\t    predicted depth →  higher perplexity → lower quality。但correlation仅0.473（非0.9+）说明depth和PPL\n863\t    不是redundant measures——depth捕捉的是distributional degradation pattern（如 surprisal\n864\t    variance compression），而PPL是point estimate of generation quality。 partial correlation（depth\n865\t    vs AlignScore controlling for PPL）= -0.198仍显著， 证明depth captures quality dimensions\n866\t    beyond PPL alone。AlignScore的负相关（-0.412） 表示higher depth → lower alignment/coherence，符合model\n867\t    collapse的预期。 predicted depth distribution的heavy left skew（d4+合计仅2.4%）也合理——deeply  recursive\n868\t    content在wild web上确实稀少（但不是zero），这正是graduated curation 的application场景。\n869\t\n870\t    '\n871\t  tables:\n872\t  - name: 'Table: Wild-data correlation results'\n873\t    content: '| Quality Proxy | Spearman ρ | p-value | Direction |\n874\t\n875\t      |---------------|-----------|---------|-----------|\n876\t\n877\t      | Perplexity | +0.473 | <1e-10 | higher depth → higher PPL |\n878\t\n879\t      | AlignScore | -0.412 | <1e-8 | higher depth → lower alignment |\n880\t\n881\t      | Partial (depth\\|PPL) vs AlignScore | -0.198 | <1e-5 | depth adds info beyond\n882\t      PPL |\n883\t\n884\t      '\n885\t  figures_description:\n886\t  - Predicted depth distribution histogram：x轴=predicted depth, y轴=percentage， 展示expected\n887\t    left-skewed distribution\n888\t  - Depth vs PPL violin plot：每个predicted depth bin的PPL分布，展示上升趋势 但overlapping distributions\n889\t  analysis: Wild-data calibration提供了ecological validity的初步证据。DCOL scores在无标签 数据上与quality\n890\t    proxies的correlation pattern完全符合model collapse理论的预测。 partial correlation的显著性（-0.198,\n891\t    p<1e-5）是最重要的结果——它证明depth不是 PPL的redundant reformulation，而是一个complementary quality\n892\t    dimension，这为 graduated curation的实际部署提供了theoretical justification。Limitation应在paper\n893\t    中明确说明：wild data没有ground-truth depth，这些correlations只验证score semantics， 不验证calibration\n894\t    accuracy。\n895\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"57df35a8-7776-42f2-9a89-3def6408fbf8","uuid":"9f5106ab-476d-4547-8d11-2fc7294a4ab7","timestamp":"2026-05-14T14:40:10.664Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513_2/projects/recursive_gen_depth_est/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260514T140607/best/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: '原始framing完全成立，三条claim均以强形式呈现。Headline: \"DCOL achieves ~72% 6-class\n  accuracy with ~60% cross-model generalization, while the best baseline achieves\n  only ~62%.\" EDD≥4证明细粒度深度区分有实际科学意义，不是trivial的binary问题。Atlas和EDD作为独立科学贡献 完全站住。每个DCOL组件贡献+2-4pp的ablation增益自证方法novelty。graduated\n  curation显著优于 binary filtering（7%+ PPL改善），proof-of-concept scope足够支撑claim 3。跨模型泛化60%+\n  是关键亮点——表明深度退化信号具有model-agnostic的不变成分。\n\n  '\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: OLMo-1B Recursive Chain (5 depths × 3 strategies)\n  plan_id: plan_002\n  description: '在OLMo-1B上生成递归链（depth 0-3，3种解码策略：nucleus p=0.95, temperature τ=0.9,  top-k\n    k=50），提取19维统计特征，训练RF分类器进行4-class深度估计。 验证退化信号在non-Pythia架构上的复现性。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    full_4class_acc: 0.759\n    full_4class_acc_ci:\n    - 0.745\n    - 0.773\n    full_mae: 0.258\n    full_auc_0v1: 0.995\n    full_auc_1v2: 0.844\n    full_auc_2v3: 0.783\n    filtered_4class_acc: 0.793\n    filtered_mae: 0.221\n    best_model: RandomForest\n    top_features:\n    - var_surprisal\n    - mean_ppl\n    - p90_ppl\n    - p75_ppl\n    - mean_surprisal\n    feature_dim: 19\n    sample_count_per_depth: ~5000\n  result_rationale: 'OLMo-1B使用不同于Pythia的架构（基于LLaMA-style rotary PE而非GPT-NeoX的learned\n    PE） 和训练数据（Dolma vs The Pile），但递归退化的核心机制——反复采样导致分布收缩——是 architecture-agnostic的。var_surprisal之所以仍是top\n    feature，是因为递归生成从高信息 量token的分布中反复re-sampling，这个过程在任何自回归LM中都会压缩surprisal的方差。 4-class\n    acc略低于Pythia（75.9% vs 78.2%）因为OLMo-1B容量更小（1B vs 1.4B）， 每一步退化幅度更大但更不规则，增加了相邻深度的混淆。AUC\n    0v1仍接近1.0因为human vs  first-gen的gap在所有模型中都是最大的。2v3 AUC=0.783低于Pythia的0.801，反映OLMo\n    在深层递归时退化轨迹的噪声更大。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Per-model 4-class RF results (alongside Pythia)'\n    content: '| Model | 4-class Acc | MAE | AUC(0v1) | AUC(1v2) | AUC(2v3) |\n\n      |-------|-------------|------|----------|----------|----------|\n\n      | Pythia-1.4B | 78.2 | 0.237 | 0.998 | 0.861 | 0.801 |\n\n      | OLMo-1B | 75.9 | 0.258 | 0.995 | 0.844 | 0.783 |\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - Feature importance对比图：Pythia vs OLMo的19维特征RF importance排名， 展示var_surprisal在两个模型中均居首位，但OLMo中mean_ppl相对权重上升\n  analysis: 'OLMo-1B确认退化信号的跨架构复现性。核心发现：(1) var_surprisal在non-Pythia模型中 同样是最强特征；(2)\n    相邻深度AUC单调递减模式一致（0v1>>1v2>>2v3）；(3) 绝对性能 略低但仍远高于chance（25%）。特征重要性排名的微小差异（mean_ppl在OLMo中更重要）\n    反映训练数据分布的差异——Dolma的文本分布更均匀，使得mean PPL的深度区分力相对增强。\n\n    '\n- name: GPT-2 XL 1.5B Recursive Chain (5 depths × 3 strategies)\n  plan_id: plan_003\n  description: '在GPT-2 XL（1.5B）上生成递归链，提取特征并训练RF。GPT-2 XL是model collapse 文献中最常用的模型（Drayson\n    et al.），使结果直接可比。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    full_4class_acc: 0.748\n    full_4class_acc_ci:\n    - 0.733\n    - 0.762\n    full_mae: 0.27\n    full_auc_0v1: 0.993\n    full_auc_1v2: 0.837\n    full_auc_2v3: 0.771\n    filtered_4class_acc: 0.781\n    filtered_mae: 0.233\n    best_model: RandomForest\n    top_features:\n    - var_surprisal\n    - p90_ppl\n    - mean_ppl\n    - mean_surprisal\n    - var_ppl\n    feature_dim: 19\n    sample_count_per_depth: ~5000\n  result_rationale: 'GPT-2 XL（1.5B）是三个模型中最大的，更大的capacity意味着每一步递归生成保留更多 原始分布的信息，因此相邻深度之间的退化幅度更小、更难区分。这解释了4-class\n    acc最低 （74.8%）和AUC 2v3最低（0.771）。但信号仍然存在且强劲——核心假设成立：递归退化 是一个universal现象，不依赖于特定模型。var_surprisal仍是top\n    feature因为surprisal 方差的压缩是递归采样的数学必然（每一步都是从前一步的分布中re-sample，方差单调非增）。 GPT-2 XL训练于WebText（高质量web文本），其退化起点更高，每步degradation更gradual，\n    所以AUC曲线整体更平缓。var_ppl进入top5（取代p75_ppl）反映GPT-2 XL的perplexity 分布在递归中的变化更多体现在variance而非quantile\n    shift上。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Complete 3-model 4-class RF results'\n    content: '| Model | 4-class Acc | MAE | AUC(0v1) | AUC(1v2) | AUC(2v3) |\n\n      |-------|-------------|------|----------|----------|----------|\n\n      | Pythia-1.4B | 78.2 | 0.237 | 0.998 | 0.861 | 0.801 |\n\n      | OLMo-1B | 75.9 | 0.258 | 0.995 | 0.844 | 0.783 |\n\n      | GPT-2 XL | 74.8 | 0.270 | 0.993 | 0.837 | 0.771 |\n\n      | Pooled mean | 76.3 | 0.255 | 0.995 | 0.847 | 0.785 |\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - 三模型AUC衰减曲线对比：x轴=adjacent pair (0v1, 1v2, 2v3)，y轴=AUC， 三条线形状一致（单调递减）但GPT-2 XL整体更低更平缓\n  analysis: 'GPT-2 XL的结果完成了3-model benchmark的feature-level验证。关键观察：(1) 三个模型 的退化轨迹定性一致——AUC单调递减，var_surprisal始终是最强特征；(2)\n    模型capacity与 退化速率呈负相关（OLMo 1B退化最快 > Pythia 1.4B > GPT-2 XL 1.5B），符合直觉； (3) 即使最弱的GPT-2\n    XL信号仍远高于chance，证明ordinal depth estimation在all  tested models上可行。pooled 4-class\n    acc 76.3%为DCOL提供了strong feature baseline。\n\n    '\n- name: 'DCOL Training: DeBERTa-v3-large with Learnable Margins Contrastive Loss'\n  plan_id: plan_004\n  description: '在pooled 3-model × 3-strategy benchmark上训练DCOL（DeBERTa-v3-large encoder\n    +  learnable non-uniform margins contrastive ordinal loss）。6-class设置（depth 0-5，\n    结合plan_011扩展数据）。三个text-specific modifications：strategy-aware margin  conditioning,\n    surprisal-augmented anchors, non-uniform learnable margins。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    dcol_6class_acc_pooled: 0.722\n    dcol_6class_acc_ci:\n    - 0.71\n    - 0.734\n    mae_6class: 0.289\n    per_class_acc:\n      d0: 0.912\n      d1: 0.793\n      d2: 0.684\n      d3: 0.618\n      d4: 0.582\n      d5: 0.548\n    per_class_f1:\n      d0: 0.903\n      d1: 0.781\n      d2: 0.672\n      d3: 0.605\n      d4: 0.569\n      d5: 0.531\n    adjacent_auc:\n      d0v1: 0.998\n      d1v2: 0.912\n      d2v3: 0.863\n      d3v4: 0.831\n      d4v5: 0.794\n    learned_margin_ratios:\n    - 1.0\n    - 0.68\n    - 0.52\n    - 0.41\n    - 0.35\n    training_epochs: 8\n    best_lr: 2.0e-05\n    embedding_dim: 256\n  result_rationale: 'DCOL在6-class上达到72.2%（chance=16.7%），核心原因有三：(1) learnable non-uniform  margins捕捉到了真实的退化几何——学到的margin\n    ratios（1.0, 0.68, 0.52, 0.41, 0.35） 反映depth 0→1间距最大、逐步缩小的真实结构，这与Atlas中观察到的non-uniform\n    inter-depth  distance完全吻合；(2) surprisal-augmented anchors将统计特征直接注入对比学习的anchor  selection，使模型能利用var_surprisal等最强信号引导embedding空间的结构；(3)\n    DeBERTa-v3 的disentangled attention机制擅长捕捉细粒度的文本统计模式。per-class acc从d0的91.2% 单调递减到d5的54.8%，符合预期——深层递归之间的文本特征差异确实在缩小。MAE=0.289意味着\n    平均预测误差不到0.3个depth level，在实际应用中非常精确。adjacent AUC从0v1的0.998到 4v5的0.794全部>0.75，说明即使在最深层仍有可分辨的信号。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: DCOL 6-class main results'\n    content: '| Metric | Value |\n\n      |--------|-------|\n\n      | 6-class Accuracy | 72.2% |\n\n      | MAE | 0.289 |\n\n      | Macro-F1 | 0.677 |\n\n      | AUC (0v1) | 0.998 |\n\n      | AUC (4v5) | 0.794 |\n\n      '\n  - name: 'Table: Per-class accuracy and F1'\n    content: '| Depth | Accuracy | F1 | Support |\n\n      |-------|----------|----|---------|\n\n      | d0 | 91.2 | 90.3 | ~5000 |\n\n      | d1 | 79.3 | 78.1 | ~5000 |\n\n      | d2 | 68.4 | 67.2 | ~5000 |\n\n      | d3 | 61.8 | 60.5 | ~5000 |\n\n      | d4 | 58.2 | 56.9 | ~5000 |\n\n      | d5 | 54.8 | 53.1 | ~5000 |\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - Confusion matrix heatmap：6×6矩阵展示ordinal structure——误分类集中在相邻depth， 几乎没有跨2个以上depth的误分类，证明DCOL学到了有意义的ordinal\n    embedding\n  - Learned margin visualization：5个学到的margin值（normalized）vs Atlas中实际的inter-depth feature\n    distance对比，展示高度正相关\n  analysis: 'DCOL的6-class 72.2%大幅超越chance（16.7%）和feature-only RF baseline（pooled ~63%\n    换算到6-class）。confusion matrix展示清晰的ordinal结构——d0几乎不会被误分类为d3+， 误分类集中在±1 depth，MAE=0.289量化了这一点。学到的margin\n    ratios与Atlas的实际 inter-depth distance高度一致（Pearson r>0.95），证明learnable margins确实捕捉到了\n    真实的退化几何，而非随机收敛。这是DCOL相对于fixed-margin方法的核心优势所在。\n\n    '\n- name: Leave-One-Model-Out Cross-Model Generalization\n  plan_id: plan_005\n  description: '3轮leave-one-model-out实验：每轮在2个模型家族上训练DCOL，在第3个模型上测试。 这是cross-model\n    generalization claim的核心验证。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    loo_6class_acc:\n      hold_out_pythia: 0.618\n      hold_out_olmo: 0.573\n      hold_out_gpt2xl: 0.612\n    loo_6class_acc_mean: 0.601\n    loo_6class_acc_ci:\n    - 0.576\n    - 0.626\n    loo_mae:\n      hold_out_pythia: 0.342\n      hold_out_olmo: 0.381\n      hold_out_gpt2xl: 0.35\n    loo_mae_mean: 0.358\n    loo_adjacent_auc_mean:\n      d0v1: 0.983\n      d1v2: 0.859\n      d2v3: 0.798\n      d3v4: 0.762\n      d4v5: 0.724\n    gate_check: PASS (mean 60.1% > 45% threshold)\n  result_rationale: '60.1%的跨模型泛化准确率（chance=16.7%）证明深度退化信号具有跨模型家族的不变成分。 核心原因：var_surprisal等top\n    features反映的是递归采样的数学性质（分布反复re-sampling 导致variance压缩），这个过程不依赖于特定模型的参数。hold-out OLMo表现最差（57.3%）\n    因为OLMo的架构（rotary PE + SwiGLU）与训练集中的Pythia（learned PE + GeLU）和 GPT-2 XL（learned\n    PE + GeLU）差异最大，退化曲线的rate不同增加了泛化难度。hold-out  GPT-2 XL反而表现不错（61.2%）因为虽然它是最大的模型，但Pythia+OLMo的训练信号\n    覆盖了更快和中等的退化速率，对GPT-2 XL较慢的退化有一定外推能力。泛化损失主要集中在 deep depths（d4v5 AUC从in-distribution的0.794降到LOO的0.724），浅层d0v1仍保持\n    0.983，说明human vs synthetic的信号高度model-agnostic。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Leave-one-model-out 6-class results'\n    content: '| Held-out Model | 6-class Acc | MAE | Δ vs in-dist |\n\n      |----------------|-------------|------|-------------|\n\n      | Pythia-1.4B | 61.8 | 0.342 | -10.4pp |\n\n      | OLMo-1B | 57.3 | 0.381 | -14.9pp |\n\n      | GPT-2 XL | 61.2 | 0.350 | -11.0pp |\n\n      | Mean | 60.1 | 0.358 | -12.1pp |\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - Per-depth AUC对比图：in-distribution vs LOO mean，展示泛化损失主要在deep depths\n  - 3-model embedding space t-SNE：不同模型的相同depth样本在embedding空间中的重叠程度\n  analysis: 'LOO mean 60.1%显著超过research-phase gate（45%），验证了跨模型泛化的核心假设。 OLMo的泛化最差这一结果本身具有科学价值——提示架构差异（而非仅训练数据差异）是跨模型\n    泛化的主要瓶颈。in-dist vs LOO的12pp gap可以在paper中honest地讨论为\"substantial  but expected\"——完美泛化不现实，但60%仍远高于所有non-oracle\n    baselines。\n\n    '\n- name: 'Depth Degradation Atlas: Feature Monotonicity, EDD, Cross-Model Heatmaps'\n  plan_id: plan_006\n  description: '系统性分析所有19维特征在3模型×3策略×6深度上的演化规律。计算per-feature monotonicity  score，确定EDD\n    boundary，生成cross-model/strategy heatmaps。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    edd_per_combo:\n      pythia_nucleus: 5\n      pythia_temperature: 4\n      pythia_topk: 4\n      olmo_nucleus: 4\n      olmo_temperature: 4\n      olmo_topk: 4\n      gpt2xl_nucleus: 4\n      gpt2xl_temperature: 4\n      gpt2xl_topk: 3\n    edd_median: 4\n    edd_range:\n    - 3\n    - 5\n    feature_monotonicity_top5:\n      var_surprisal: 0.961\n      p90_ppl: 0.928\n      mean_ppl: 0.907\n      mean_surprisal: 0.891\n      p75_ppl: 0.873\n    feature_monotonicity_top5_mean: 0.912\n    min_adjacent_auc_within_edd: 0.812\n    non_monotonic_features:\n    - burstiness\n    - type_token_ratio\n    strongest_cross_model_invariant: var_surprisal\n    inter_depth_distance_ratio_d01_vs_d34: 2.83\n  result_rationale: 'EDD median=4意味着在9个model×strategy组合中，多数能区分到depth 4（即d3 vs d4仍可分辨），\n    这远超\"trivial binary\"的担忧。var_surprisal的monotonicity=0.961（接近完美单调）是因为 每一轮递归生成都是从前一轮的经验分布中采样，数学上这导致surprisal的variance单调非增——\n    极端token（高surprisal或低surprisal）在每一轮中被progressively smoothed out。 inter-depth distance\n    ratio d01 vs d34 = 2.83证实了非均匀性——depth 0→1的特征空间 距离是depth 3→4的2.83倍，这正是DCOL learnable\n    margins需要捕捉的结构。GPT-2 XL ×  top-k的EDD=3是9个组合中最低的，因为top-k采样在大模型上限制了token选择范围，加速了\n    浅层退化但也加速了深层饱和。nucleus在所有模型上EDD最高（4-5），因为nucleus的动态 truncation保留了更多分布信息。burstiness和type_token_ratio是少数非单调特征，因为\n    递归生成可能在中间深度出现temporary diversity recovery（Drayson et al.  报告的non-monotonic现象），但这不影响overall\n    discrimination。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: EDD matrix (model × strategy)'\n    content: '| Model | nucleus | temperature | top-k | Mean |\n\n      |-------|---------|-------------|-------|------|\n\n      | Pythia-1.4B | 5 | 4 | 4 | 4.33 |\n\n      | OLMo-1B | 4 | 4 | 4 | 4.00 |\n\n      | GPT-2 XL | 4 | 4 | 3 | 3.67 |\n\n      | Mean | 4.33 | 4.00 | 3.67 | 4.00 |\n\n      '\n  - name: 'Table: Feature monotonicity scores (top 10)'\n    content: '| Rank | Feature | Mono. Score | Best Model | Worst Model |\n\n      |------|---------|-------------|------------|-------------|\n\n      | 1 | var_surprisal | 0.961 | Pythia | GPT-2 XL |\n\n      | 2 | p90_ppl | 0.928 | OLMo | GPT-2 XL |\n\n      | 3 | mean_ppl | 0.907 | Pythia | OLMo |\n\n      | 4 | mean_surprisal | 0.891 | Pythia | GPT-2 XL |\n\n      | 5 | p75_ppl | 0.873 | OLMo | GPT-2 XL |\n\n      | 6 | var_ppl | 0.856 | GPT-2 XL | OLMo |\n\n      | 7 | p50_ppl | 0.841 | Pythia | GPT-2 XL |\n\n      | 8 | entropy_unigram | 0.823 | OLMo | Pythia |\n\n      | 9 | p25_ppl | 0.794 | OLMo | GPT-2 XL |\n\n      | 10 | zipf_alpha | 0.771 | Pythia | OLMo |\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - Atlas主图：3×3 heatmap grid（行=model, 列=strategy），每个cell展示19维特征 随depth 0→5的z-score变化轨迹，用颜色编码方向和幅度。var_surprisal行在所有9个\n    cell中显示一致的深蓝色递减带\n  - EDD boundary可视化：per-combo的adjacent AUC曲线，水平虚线标注threshold， AUC落到threshold以下的depth即为EDD\n    boundary\n  - Inter-depth distance散点图：所有adjacent depth pair的embedding距离， 标注d0→1远大于d3→4的非均匀结构\n  analysis: 'Atlas的三大发现：(1) EDD median=4证明深度估计不是trivial的binary问题——至少4个 adjacent depth\n    pair可被可靠区分，这为6-class formulation提供了科学依据；(2)  var_surprisal的near-perfect monotonicity（0.961）和cross-model\n    consistency 使其成为depth estimation的\"universal biomarker\"；(3) inter-depth distance的\n    强非均匀性（d01/d34 ratio=2.83）直接motivates DCOL的learnable margins设计—— fixed-margin方法在这种geometry下必然suboptimal。Atlas作为独立科学贡献的价值在于：\n    即使不做任何classification，这些findings也推进了对model collapse dynamics的理解。\n\n    '\n- name: Leave-One-Strategy-Out Robustness\n  plan_id: plan_007\n  description: '3轮leave-one-strategy-out实验：每轮在2种decoding策略上训练DCOL，在第3种策略上测试。 验证DCOL表征的strategy-invariance。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    loso_6class_acc:\n      hold_out_nucleus: 0.681\n      hold_out_temperature: 0.658\n      hold_out_topk: 0.673\n    loso_6class_acc_mean: 0.671\n    loso_mae_mean: 0.312\n    loso_delta_vs_in_dist: -5.1\n  result_rationale: 'Strategy-out mean 67.1%高于model-out mean 60.1%，符合预期——不同decoding策略共享\n    同一个模型的参数和vocabulary，差异仅在于采样分布的truncation/reshaping方式。 hold-out temperature最差（65.8%）因为temperature\n    scaling改变了整个logit分布的 shape（除以τ后softmax变平或变尖），产生的文本统计模式与nucleus（dynamic truncation）\n    和top-k（hard truncation）不同。hold-out nucleus反而最好（68.1%）因为nucleus的 动态阈值使其特征分布位于temperature和top-k之间，被后两者的训练数据较好覆盖。\n    strategy conditioning module（plan_010将ablate的组件）在这里的贡献是：当conditioning 被移除时，strategy-out性能将下降更多，说明该组件确实在学习strategy-specific的\n    adjustment。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Leave-one-strategy-out results'\n    content: '| Held-out Strategy | 6-class Acc | MAE | Δ vs in-dist |\n\n      |-------------------|-------------|------|-------------|\n\n      | nucleus (p=0.95) | 68.1 | 0.298 | -4.1pp |\n\n      | temperature (τ=0.9) | 65.8 | 0.325 | -6.4pp |\n\n      | top-k (k=50) | 67.3 | 0.313 | -4.9pp |\n\n      | Mean | 67.1 | 0.312 | -5.1pp |\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - Strategy transfer matrix：3×3矩阵展示每对策略之间的transfer accuracy， 对角线是in-distribution性能\n  analysis: 'Strategy-out gap（5.1pp）约为model-out gap（12.1pp）的一半，证明decoding strategy\n    对退化信号的影响远小于model architecture/training data。这是positive的结果—— 实际应用中，我们更可能遇到未知模型（而非未知策略），model-out的60%+泛化更重要。\n    temperature transfer最差可以在paper中作为limitation提及，同时指出即使worst-case 65.8%仍远高于chance。\n\n    '\n- name: DeBERTa End-to-End Classifier (text → depth, no handcrafted features)\n  plan_id: plan_008\n  description: 'DeBERTa-v3-large直接从raw text预测depth（标准fine-tuning with classification\n    head）， 不使用手工统计特征。对比feature-based DCOL和end-to-end方法。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    e2e_6class_acc: 0.703\n    e2e_6class_acc_ci:\n    - 0.69\n    - 0.716\n    e2e_mae: 0.314\n    e2e_vs_dcol_delta: -1.9\n    e2e_cross_model_loo_mean: 0.524\n    e2e_cross_model_loo_delta_vs_dcol: -7.7\n    training_epochs: 5\n    best_lr: 1.0e-05\n  result_rationale: 'End-to-end（70.3%）略低于DCOL（72.2%），delta仅1.9pp，说明DeBERTa能隐式学到 类似var_surprisal的统计模式。但差距存在是因为：(1)\n    DCOL的surprisal-augmented anchors 使用外部reference model（Pythia-1.4B自身）计算的token-level\n    surprisal，这个信号 无法从text tokens alone隐式获得；(2) learnable margins作为architectural inductive  bias比CE\n    loss head的implicit ordinal更有效。关键差异在cross-model LOO：end-to-end LOO仅52.4%（vs DCOL的60.1%），差距扩大到7.7pp。这是因为end-to-end方法更容易\n    overfit到训练模型的idiosyncratic patterns（如特定的token偏好），而feature-based  DCOL的hand-crafted\n    features天然具有更强的model-invariance。这个结果validates了 feature-based + contrastive learning的设计选择。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Feature-based DCOL vs End-to-End comparison'\n    content: '| Method | In-dist Acc | LOO Acc | MAE | Interpretable? |\n\n      |--------|-------------|---------|------|----------------|\n\n      | DCOL (features) | 72.2 | 60.1 | 0.289 | Yes |\n\n      | DeBERTa E2E | 70.3 | 52.4 | 0.314 | No |\n\n      | Δ | +1.9pp | +7.7pp | -0.025 | — |\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - In-dist vs cross-model scatter：两种方法在9个combo上的per-combo accuracy， 展示DCOL在所有combo上更一致，E2E的方差更大\n  analysis: 'End-to-end vs feature-based的对比是paper story的重要组成部分。In-dist差距小（1.9pp） 但cross-model差距大（7.7pp）这个pattern非常有叙事价值——它证明feature\n    engineering 不是\"legacy approach\"，而是在generalization场景下有structural advantage。可以在\n    paper中argue：对于depth estimation这种需要跨模型部署的任务，feature-based +  contrastive ordinal\n    learning是superior design choice。\n\n    '\n- name: 'Baseline Battery: 7 Methods Repurposed for Depth Estimation'\n  plan_id: plan_009\n  description: '7种baseline方法在pooled 6-class benchmark上的表现。包括：binary detector特征 重定向、perplexity回归、fixed-margin\n    ordinal、标准CE、zero-shot LLM。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    baselines:\n      diveye_ordinal_reg:\n        acc_6class: 0.527\n        mae: 0.512\n      binoculars_ordinal_reg:\n        acc_6class: 0.498\n        mae: 0.548\n      ppl_regression:\n        acc_6class: 0.461\n        mae: 0.583\n      coral_fixed_margin_deberta:\n        acc_6class: 0.621\n        mae: 0.358\n      ce_deberta:\n        acc_6class: 0.598\n        mae: 0.402\n      feature_ordinal_rf:\n        acc_6class: 0.573\n        mae: 0.421\n      zeroshot_gpt4:\n        acc_6class: 0.248\n        mae: 0.891\n    best_baseline: coral_fixed_margin_deberta\n    best_baseline_acc: 0.621\n    dcol_delta_pp: 10.1\n    dcol_delta_significant: true\n    significance_test: paired bootstrap, p < 0.001\n  result_rationale: 'CORAL fixed-margin（62.1%）是最强baseline因为它至少利用了ordinal structure，但\n    fixed margins无法适应真实的non-uniform inter-depth geometry（d01 gap远大于d34 gap）， 所以比DCOL低10.1pp。CE-DeBERTa（59.8%）略低于CORAL因为CE\n    loss不编码ordinal  structure，允许d0被误分类为d5（而CORAL至少penalizes远距离错误）。DivEye和Binoculars\n    的features为binary detection设计（entropy ratio, cross-perplexity等），forced into ordinal\n    regression后信息不足——它们的features区分real/synthetic很强但不carry depth  信息。PPL regression最差（46.1%）因为perplexity和depth不是简单线性关系，中间depth\n    的PPL分布大量重叠。Zero-shot GPT-4（24.8%，接近chance 16.7%）证明depth estimation 不是一个可以通过world\n    knowledge推断的任务，需要专门的statistical features和训练。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Full baseline comparison (main results table)'\n    content: '| Method | Type | 6-class Acc | MAE | Δ vs DCOL |\n\n      |--------|------|-------------|------|-----------|\n\n      | DCOL (ours) | Contrastive ordinal | 72.2 | 0.289 | — |\n\n      | CORAL-DeBERTa | Fixed-margin ordinal | 62.1 | 0.358 | -10.1pp |\n\n      | CE-DeBERTa | Standard classification | 59.8 | 0.402 | -12.4pp |\n\n      | Feature RF+CORAL | Feature ordinal | 57.3 | 0.421 | -14.9pp |\n\n      | DivEye features | Binary repurposed | 52.7 | 0.512 | -19.5pp |\n\n      | Binoculars features | Binary repurposed | 49.8 | 0.548 | -22.4pp |\n\n      | PPL regression | Direct regression | 46.1 | 0.583 | -26.1pp |\n\n      | GPT-4 zero-shot | Prompting | 24.8 | 0.891 | -47.4pp |\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - Bar chart：所有methods的6-class acc，DCOL用深色标注，baseline用浅色， 水平虚线标chance=16.7%。视觉上DCOL明显高于所有baseline\n  - MAE vs Accuracy scatter：每个method一个点，DCOL在右下角（high acc, low MAE）， 展示ordinal methods（DCOL,\n    CORAL）整体优于non-ordinal methods\n  analysis: 'DCOL相对best baseline（CORAL）的10.1pp增益在统计上高度显著（p<0.001），且这个 增益完全来自三个text-specific\n    modifications（ablation将在plan_010中量化）。 Binary detector features的低性能（49.8-52.7%）是重要的negative\n    result——证明 depth estimation确实是一个不同于binary detection的新任务，不能简单repurpose现有 工具。Zero-shot\n    GPT-4接近chance的结果有shock value，可以用在paper开头的motivation 段落：\"even state-of-the-art\n    LLMs cannot distinguish recursive depth from text  alone, highlighting the need\n    for specialized methods.\"\n\n    '\n- name: DCOL Component Ablation\n  plan_id: plan_010\n  description: '逐一移除DCOL的三个text-specific modifications，量化每个组件的贡献。 包括：surprisal-augmented\n    anchors, learnable non-uniform margins,  strategy-aware conditioning。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    full_dcol: 0.722\n    ablations:\n      w_o_surprisal_anchors:\n        acc: 0.691\n        delta: -3.1\n      w_o_learnable_margins:\n        acc: 0.683\n        delta: -3.9\n      w_o_strategy_conditioning:\n        acc: 0.7\n        delta: -2.2\n      w_o_all_three:\n        acc: 0.641\n        delta: -8.1\n    interaction_effect: 'sum of individual Δ = 9.2pp > joint Δ = 8.1pp → 1.1pp positive\n      interaction  (components partially redundant)\n\n      '\n    best_single_component: learnable_margins\n  result_rationale: 'Learnable margins贡献最大（-3.9pp when removed）因为depth geometry的非均匀性是\n    DCOL与fixed-margin methods的核心区分点——移除后退化为uniform-margin contrastive loss， 在d3-d5的密集区域大量误分类。Surprisal\n    anchors次之（-3.1pp）因为它们直接注入了 var_surprisal这个最强信号作为anchor selection的prior；移除后模型仍能从text\n    tokens 隐式学到部分信号，但效率降低。Strategy conditioning贡献最小（-2.2pp）因为三种策略 共享核心退化机制，conditioning的marginal\n    value在于fine-tune depth boundary的 strategy-specific位移。all-three-removed后的64.1%仍高于CORAL（62.1%），说明\n    DeBERTa encoder + contrastive learning framework本身也有优势（better optimization  landscape\n    vs fixed-margin ordinal）。个体Δ之和（9.2pp）略大于joint Δ（8.1pp）， 说明组件间有1.1pp的positive interaction——这合理，因为surprisal\n    anchors和learnable  margins都在利用depth geometry信息，有轻微的信息重叠。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Ablation results'\n    content: '| Configuration | 6-class Acc | Δ | MAE |\n\n      |---------------|-------------|-------|------|\n\n      | DCOL (full) | 72.2 | — | 0.289 |\n\n      | w/o surprisal anchors | 69.1 | -3.1 | 0.318 |\n\n      | w/o learnable margins | 68.3 | -3.9 | 0.331 |\n\n      | w/o strategy cond. | 70.0 | -2.2 | 0.305 |\n\n      | w/o all three | 64.1 | -8.1 | 0.382 |\n\n      | CORAL baseline | 62.1 | -10.1 | 0.358 |\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - Waterfall chart：从base contrastive（64.1%）逐步加回每个组件到full DCOL（72.2%）， 展示每个组件的累积增益\n  analysis: '所有三个组件都有显著且独立的贡献（2-4pp each），验证了DCOL的design choices不是 arbitrary的。learnable\n    margins是最关键组件——这与Atlas中观察到的strong non-uniform geometry直接对应，形成了elegant的 \"observation\n    → design → validation\" narrative。 w/o all three仍略好于CORAL（+2.0pp）提供了额外insight：contrastive\n    learning  framework本身（而非仅modifications）也对ordinal estimation有贡献，可能因为 contrastive\n    loss的pair-wise comparison比CORAL的pointwise threshold更适合 ordinal ranking。\n\n    '\n- name: Depth Extension to 5 Generations + EDD Saturation Analysis\n  plan_id: plan_011\n  description: '将Pythia递归链从depth 0-3扩展到depth 0-5（6 classes）。分析discrimination是否 在depth\n    4-5饱和。提供EDD的per-strategy细粒度分析。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    pythia_extended_auc:\n      d0v1: 0.998\n      d1v2: 0.861\n      d2v3: 0.801\n      d3v4: 0.785\n      d4v5_nucleus: 0.813\n      d4v5_temperature: 0.728\n      d4v5_topk: 0.712\n    pythia_edd:\n      nucleus: 5\n      temperature: 4\n      topk: 4\n    rf_6class_acc_pythia: 0.698\n    rf_6class_acc_ci:\n    - 0.682\n    - 0.714\n    rf_6class_mae: 0.331\n    saturation_depth: 4\n    feature_saturation:\n      var_surprisal_slope_d4_d5: -0.031\n      var_surprisal_slope_d0_d1: -0.187\n      slope_ratio: 6.03\n  result_rationale: 'Pythia在nucleus下EDD=5（d4v5 AUC=0.813 > 0.75 threshold），说明即使到depth\n    5 仍有可辨别的退化信号。这是best tier的关键指标——证明递归退化不是在depth 2-3就饱和 的trivial现象。但d4v5的AUC（0.813）已显著低于d0v1（0.998），且temperature和\n    top-k下d4v5 AUC分别为0.728和0.712（低于threshold），说明saturation正在发生。 feature saturation分析揭示原因：var_surprisal在d4→d5的斜率（-0.031）仅为\n    d0→d1斜率（-0.187）的1/6，意味着信号幅度在deep depths急剧缩小。6-class RF acc 从4-class的78.2%降到69.8%，反映增加d4和d5后的分类难度增大。saturation_depth=4\n    表示大多数特征在depth 4后变化速率趋近于零，这与EDD median=4一致。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Extended depth adjacent AUC (Pythia)'\n    content: '| Pair | nucleus | temperature | top-k | Mean |\n\n      |------|---------|-------------|-------|------|\n\n      | d0v1 | 0.998 | 0.996 | 0.995 | 0.996 |\n\n      | d1v2 | 0.871 | 0.856 | 0.849 | 0.859 |\n\n      | d2v3 | 0.813 | 0.796 | 0.788 | 0.799 |\n\n      | d3v4 | 0.798 | 0.781 | 0.774 | 0.784 |\n\n      | d4v5 | 0.813 | 0.728 | 0.712 | 0.751 |\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - AUC衰减曲线（3策略）：x轴=depth pair, y轴=AUC，展示nucleus在deep depth 保持最高AUC，top-k最低。水平虚线标EDD\n    threshold\n  - Feature slope heatmap：每个特征在每个相邻depth pair的normalized change rate， 展示progressive\n    saturation pattern\n  analysis: 'Depth extension为6-class benchmark提供了科学依据：EDD=4-5证明不是所有depth pair 都trivially\n    separable也不是depth 2就饱和。Nucleus strategy在deep depth维持最高 discrimination的发现可以在paper中给出mechanistic解释：nucleus的dynamic\n    vocabulary  truncation保留了更多distributional diversity per generation step。 d4v5\n    AUC在nucleus下的slight recovery（0.813 vs d3v4的0.798）看似非单调， 但实际上在error bars内是consistent——这不是Drayson\n    et al.报告的non-monotonic  degradation，而是统计波动。\n\n    '\n- name: 'Granularity Ablation: Binary / 3-class / 4-class / 6-class'\n  plan_id: plan_012\n  description: '在相同数据和DCOL方法上比较不同粒度的depth estimation性能。 展示ordinal framing相对于binary的marginal\n    benefit。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    dcol_acc_by_granularity:\n      binary_d0_vs_rest: 0.961\n      binary_d0d1_vs_d2plus: 0.938\n      three_class: 0.845\n      four_class: 0.793\n      six_class: 0.722\n    mae_by_granularity:\n      binary_d0_vs_rest: 0.039\n      three_class: 0.165\n      four_class: 0.221\n      six_class: 0.289\n    ordinal_benefit: '4-class vs binary: 4-class provides 3 additional depth distinctions\n      with only  16.8pp accuracy cost; MAE metric shows ordinal errors are small\n\n      '\n  result_rationale: 'Binary detection是near-solved（96.1%）——这符合MVP中d0v1 AUC=0.998的观察，\n    human vs any-synthetic的gap巨大。3-class（84.5%）加入了\"shallow vs deep synthetic\" 的区分，仍然很准确。4-class（79.3%）匹配MVP的78.2%（DCOL优于RF\n    1.1pp）。 6-class（72.2%）展示了fine-grained depth estimation的可行性。性能从96.1%单调递减 到72.2%，但递减速率本身在减缓——从binary到3-class降11.6pp，从4-class到6-class仅降\n    7.1pp——说明更细粒度的depth distinction在变得更难但return没有collapse。这条曲线的 shape本身就是一个scientifically\n    interesting finding：如果曲线在4-class就断崖式 下降（如降到50%），那6-class formulation就不合理；现在72.2%仍远高于chance=16.7%，\n    证明6-class formulation是well-motivated的。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Accuracy across granularity levels'\n    content: '| Granularity | Classes | Chance | DCOL Acc | Above Chance |\n\n      |-------------|---------|--------|---------|--------------|\n\n      | Binary | 2 | 50.0% | 96.1% | +46.1pp |\n\n      | 3-class | 3 | 33.3% | 84.5% | +51.2pp |\n\n      | 4-class | 4 | 25.0% | 79.3% | +54.3pp |\n\n      | 6-class | 6 | 16.7% | 72.2% | +55.5pp |\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - Accuracy vs granularity曲线：x轴=number of classes, y轴=accuracy (left) 和 above-chance\n    accuracy (right)。above-chance accuracy实际上随粒度增加而 微增，是paper的亮点数据点\n  analysis: 'Above-chance accuracy从binary的46.1pp微增到6-class的55.5pp，这是一个非常elegant 的结果——说明DCOL在更细粒度下实际上extract了更多的depth\n    information（按relative  scale衡量）。这个finding可以作为paper中\"Why ordinal and not just binary?\"的\n    definitive answer：not only does finer granularity retain high accuracy, the information\n    gain per additional class remains positive。\n\n    '\n- name: Downstream Graduated Curation vs Binary Filtering\n  plan_id: plan_013\n  description: 'Proof-of-concept downstream application：用DCOL predicted depth作为data\n    curation signal，比较graduated weighting（1/k权重）vs binary filtering vs no filtering\n    对1B model fine-tuning的影响。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    no_filtering_ppl: 26.14\n    binary_filtering_ppl: 24.52\n    graduated_weighting_ppl: 22.78\n    ppl_reduction_vs_binary_pct: 7.1\n    ppl_reduction_vs_no_filter_pct: 12.85\n    graduated_retained_data_pct: 92.3\n    binary_retained_data_pct: 71.6\n    sensitivity_analysis:\n      weight_1_over_k: 22.78\n      weight_1_over_k_squared: 23.01\n      weight_exp_neg_k: 22.91\n      weight_linear_decay: 23.15\n    best_weighting: 1/k\n    training_tokens: 500M\n    eval_set: held-out RedPajama subset\n  result_rationale: 'Graduated weighting（PPL 22.78）优于binary filtering（PPL 24.52），改善7.1%，\n    原因有二：(1) binary filtering粗暴丢弃所有synthetic data（丢弃28.4%数据）， 但其中depth 1的shallow synthetic\n    content质量仍然很高，丢弃它们是unnecessary  data waste；graduated weighting保留92.3%的数据，仅down-weight\n    deep recursive  content，保留了shallow synthetic的positive contribution。(2) 1/k权重scheme\n    恰好近似了退化severity的reciprocal——depth 1内容几乎不down-weight（×1.0）， depth 3内容weight=0.33，depth\n    5内容weight=0.2，这与Atlas中观察到的质量退化 曲线形状吻合。sensitivity analysis显示不同权重函数的差异较小（PPL 22.78-23.15），\n    说明graduated的核心优势来自\"保留而非丢弃shallow synthetic\"的大方向，而非具体 权重函数的形式。no-filtering的PPL最高（26.14）确认了deep\n    recursive content 确实harmful——不做任何过滤是worst choice。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Downstream curation comparison'\n    content: '| Strategy | PPL↓ | Data Retained | Δ vs Binary |\n\n      |----------|------|---------------|-------------|\n\n      | No filtering | 26.14 | 100% | — |\n\n      | Binary (remove synthetic) | 24.52 | 71.6% | baseline |\n\n      | Graduated 1/k | 22.78 | 92.3% | -7.1% PPL |\n\n      | Graduated 1/k² | 23.01 | 92.3% | -6.2% PPL |\n\n      | Graduated exp(-k) | 22.91 | 92.3% | -6.6% PPL |\n\n      | Linear decay | 23.15 | 92.3% | -5.6% PPL |\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - PPL vs data retention trade-off曲线：binary是一个点（71.6%, 24.52）， graduated schemes在更高retention（92.3%）下实现更低PPL，展示Pareto\n    improvement\n  analysis: '7.1% PPL improvement over binary filtering在proof-of-concept scope下是convincing的。\n    关键insight不是\"哪个权重函数最好\"（差异小），而是\"graduated approach本身是a better  paradigm than binary\"——它保留了20.7%更多的数据同时获得了更低的PPL。这个finding\n    直接supports claim 3，且与claim 1和claim 2形成完整链条：Atlas发现depth有意义的 结构→DCOL能准确预测depth→depth-aware\n    curation能改善downstream quality。 paper中~1 page的proof-of-concept scope足够传达这个message。\n\n    '\n- name: 7B Cross-Scale Probe (Qwen2.5-7B or Llama-3.1-8B)\n  plan_id: plan_014\n  description: '在7B模型上生成3-depth递归链（depth 0-2），用在1-1.5B模型上训练的DCOL进行 depth estimation。测试scale\n    transfer。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    model_used: Llama-3.1-8B\n    depths_generated:\n    - 0\n    - 1\n    - 2\n    dcol_3class_acc: 0.712\n    dcol_3class_acc_ci:\n    - 0.688\n    - 0.736\n    mae_3class: 0.301\n    auc_0v1: 0.963\n    auc_1v2: 0.821\n    feature_monotonicity_top3:\n      var_surprisal: 0.94\n      p90_ppl: 0.89\n      mean_ppl: 0.86\n    degradation_rate_vs_small_models: 0.67\n  result_rationale: '7B模型的3-class accuracy 71.2%（chance=33.3%）证明depth signals从1-1.5B模型\n    transfer到7B模型。transfer成功的原因是核心退化特征（var_surprisal等）反映的是 递归采样的distributional dynamics而非model-specific\n    patterns。degradation_rate  0.67x意味着7B模型的退化速度约为小模型的2/3——capacity更大，每步保留更多分布信息，\n    退化更gradual。这导致adjacent depth间的feature gap更小，所以即使在3-class （比6-class简单）上accuracy也仅71.2%。AUC\n    0v1=0.963虽然低于小模型的~0.998， 但仍很高——human vs synthetic的gap在7B模型上缩小但仍robust，因为7B的生成质量\n    更高，使d0 vs d1更接近。特征单调性在7B上保持（var_surprisal=0.94），说明退化 的qualitative pattern是scale-invariant的。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Cross-scale transfer results'\n    content: '| Setting | 3-class Acc | AUC(0v1) | AUC(1v2) |\n\n      |---------|-------------|----------|----------|\n\n      | DCOL on 1-1.5B (in-dist) | 84.5 | 0.998 | 0.912 |\n\n      | DCOL on 7B (transfer) | 71.2 | 0.963 | 0.821 |\n\n      | Δ | -13.3pp | -0.035 | -0.091 |\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - Feature evolution对比：7B vs 1.4B model的depth 0-2特征轨迹，展示 qualitatively same pattern但amplitude\n    reduced in 7B\n  analysis: 'Cross-scale transfer result（71.2%）是positive但有limitation。13.3pp的transfer\n    gap 比cross-model LOO gap（12.1pp）略大，说明scale difference比architecture difference\n    影响稍大。Paper中应honest地说：DCOL trained on small models has meaningful but  imperfect\n    transfer to 7B。7B上退化更慢的发现本身有scientific value——it suggests  larger models are more\n    resilient to model collapse per recursion step, but still  degrade eventually。\n\n    '\n- name: 'Wild-Data Calibration: DCOL Scores on RedPajama/Dolma'\n  plan_id: plan_015\n  description: '在无ground-truth depth标签的wild data（RedPajama/Dolma样本）上运行DCOL， 分析predicted\n    depth scores与quality proxies（perplexity, AlignScore）的correlation。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    dataset_samples: 50000\n    predicted_depth_distribution:\n      d0_pct: 72.3\n      d1_pct: 14.8\n      d2_pct: 7.1\n      d3_pct: 3.4\n      d4_pct: 1.6\n      d5_pct: 0.8\n    spearman_vs_ppl: 0.473\n    spearman_vs_alignscore: -0.412\n    spearman_vs_ppl_p_value: <1e-10\n    spearman_vs_alignscore_p_value: <1e-8\n    calibration_note: 'Predicted depth and quality proxies are correlated but not\n      redundant;  depth captures distributional degradation beyond what perplexity\n      alone measures\n\n      '\n    partial_corr_depth_given_ppl_vs_alignscore: -0.198\n  result_rationale: 'DCOL在wild data上预测72.3%为d0（human-written），符合预期——大部分web text仍是\n    human-authored。14.8%被预测为d1（first-gen synthetic），合理反映了当前web上AI生成 内容的比例。Spearman与PPL的正相关（0.473）符合预期：higher\n    predicted depth →  higher perplexity → lower quality。但correlation仅0.473（非0.9+）说明depth和PPL\n    不是redundant measures——depth捕捉的是distributional degradation pattern（如 surprisal\n    variance compression），而PPL是point estimate of generation quality。 partial correlation（depth\n    vs AlignScore controlling for PPL）= -0.198仍显著， 证明depth captures quality dimensions\n    beyond PPL alone。AlignScore的负相关（-0.412） 表示higher depth → lower alignment/coherence，符合model\n    collapse的预期。 predicted depth distribution的heavy left skew（d4+合计仅2.4%）也合理——deeply  recursive\n    content在wild web上确实稀少（但不是zero），这正是graduated curation 的application场景。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Wild-data correlation results'\n    content: '| Quality Proxy | Spearman ρ | p-value | Direction |\n\n      |---------------|-----------|---------|-----------|\n\n      | Perplexity | +0.473 | <1e-10 | higher depth → higher PPL |\n\n      | AlignScore | -0.412 | <1e-8 | higher depth → lower alignment |\n\n      | Partial (depth\\|PPL) vs AlignScore | -0.198 | <1e-5 | depth adds info beyond\n      PPL |\n\n      '\n  figures_description:\n  - Predicted depth distribution histogram：x轴=predicted depth, y轴=percentage， 展示expected\n    left-skewed distribution\n  - Depth vs PPL violin plot：每个predicted depth bin的PPL分布，展示上升趋势 但overlapping distributions\n  analysis: Wild-data calibration提供了ecological validity的初步证据。DCOL scores在无标签 数据上与quality\n    proxies的correlation pattern完全符合model collapse理论的预测。 partial correlation的显著性（-0.198,\n    p<1e-5）是最重要的结果——它证明depth不是 PPL的redundant reformulation，而是一个complementary quality\n    dimension，这为 graduated curation的实际部署提供了theoretical justification。Limitation应在paper\n    中明确说明：wild data没有ground-truth depth，这些correlations只验证score semantics， 不验证calibration\n    accuracy。\n","numLines":895,"startLine":1,"totalLines":895}}}
