{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BYgberytuPZHxn6QP2Fy5w","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"EMNLP 2026 reviewer guidelines review form\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"FAQ - EMNLP 2026\",\"url\":\"https://2026.emnlp.org/faq/\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2026 : The 2026 Conference on Empirical Methods in N\",\"url\":\"https://callforpaper.org/call-for-papers-emnlp-2026\"},{\"title\":\"LINGUIST List 37.972 Confs: 2026 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing (Hungary)\",\"url\":\"https://linguistlist.org/issues/37/972/\"},{\"title\":\"Instructions for Reviewers for EMNLP 2020\",\"url\":\"https://2020.emnlp.org/blog/2020-05-26-instructions-for-reviewers/\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2026 | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP%2F2026\"},{\"title\":\"Advice on Reviewing for EMNLP\",\"url\":\"https://2020.emnlp.org/blog/2020-05-17-write-good-reviews/\"},{\"title\":\"Changes to reviewer volunteering requirement and incentives in May 2025 cycle (EMNLP 2025)\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2025\"},{\"title\":\"ClimateNLP 2026\",\"url\":\"https://nlp4climate.github.io/submissionguide/\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - acl-org/emnlp-2026: Repository for the EMNLP 2026 conference · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/acl-org/emnlp-2026\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found some relevant information about EMNLP 2026 reviewer guidelines and review deadlines, though the specific review form details for 2026 are not fully available in these results.\n\nHere's what I found:\n\n## Review Deadlines\nIf you receive assignments, your reviews must be completed by July 6, or your meta-reviews by July 29.\n\n## Review Structure\nSubmissions are handled via the Open Review platform, with authors first submitting to ACL Rolling Review (ARR) to receive reviews and meta-reviews from ARR reviewers and action editors, then committing reviewed articles to EMNLP 2026 where Senior Area Chairs and Program Chairs make acceptance decisions.\n\n## General Reviewer Guidelines\nWhile specific EMNLP 2026 reviewer guidelines weren't fully detailed in the results, the search did return general guidance on reviewing for EMNLP (from 2020). The guidelines emphasize being specific in comments, constructive in advice, and evaluating papers based on their contributions rather than just comparative performance.\n\nFor the most current and detailed EMNLP 2026 reviewer guidelines and review form, I recommend checking the official EMNLP 2026 website at **2026.emnlp.org** or the OpenReview platform at **openreview.net**, which would have the specific review form criteria and detailed instructions for reviewers.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"57df35a8-7776-42f2-9a89-3def6408fbf8","uuid":"8454184b-7fcb-4a32-9bdb-4cdc76b970bf","timestamp":"2026-05-14T14:40:26.585Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"EMNLP 2026 reviewer guidelines review form","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_011ACSXEK3BpPYev3ZsCFPjV","content":[{"title":"FAQ - EMNLP 2026","url":"https://2026.emnlp.org/faq/"},{"title":"EMNLP 2026 : The 2026 Conference on Empirical Methods in N","url":"https://callforpaper.org/call-for-papers-emnlp-2026"},{"title":"LINGUIST List 37.972 Confs: 2026 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing (Hungary)","url":"https://linguistlist.org/issues/37/972/"},{"title":"Instructions for Reviewers for EMNLP 2020","url":"https://2020.emnlp.org/blog/2020-05-26-instructions-for-reviewers/"},{"title":"EMNLP 2026 | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP%2F2026"},{"title":"Advice on Reviewing for EMNLP","url":"https://2020.emnlp.org/blog/2020-05-17-write-good-reviews/"},{"title":"Changes to reviewer volunteering requirement and incentives in May 2025 cycle (EMNLP 2025)","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2025"},{"title":"ClimateNLP 2026","url":"https://nlp4climate.github.io/submissionguide/"},{"title":"EMNLP | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP"},{"title":"GitHub - acl-org/emnlp-2026: Repository for the EMNLP 2026 conference · GitHub","url":"https://github.com/acl-org/emnlp-2026"}]},"Based on the search results, I found some relevant information about EMNLP 2026 reviewer guidelines and review deadlines, though the specific review form details for 2026 are not fully available in these results.\n\nHere's what I found:\n\n## Review Deadlines\nIf you receive assignments, your reviews must be completed by July 6, or your meta-reviews by July 29.\n\n## Review Structure\nSubmissions are handled via the Open Review platform, with authors first submitting to ACL Rolling Review (ARR) to receive reviews and meta-reviews from ARR reviewers and action editors, then committing reviewed articles to EMNLP 2026 where Senior Area Chairs and Program Chairs make acceptance decisions.\n\n## General Reviewer Guidelines\nWhile specific EMNLP 2026 reviewer guidelines weren't fully detailed in the results, the search did return general guidance on reviewing for EMNLP (from 2020). The guidelines emphasize being specific in comments, constructive in advice, and evaluating papers based on their contributions rather than just comparative performance.\n\nFor the most current and detailed EMNLP 2026 reviewer guidelines and review form, I recommend checking the official EMNLP 2026 website at **2026.emnlp.org** or the OpenReview platform at **openreview.net**, which would have the specific review form criteria and detailed instructions for reviewers."],"durationSeconds":6.336807717}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0146QARTnc8V6HUtVUiz9CtW","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"EMNLP 2025 review form scoring rubric reviewer guidelines\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Criteria for Determining Irresponsible Reviewers - EMNLP 2025\",\"url\":\"https://2025.emnlp.org/reviewer-policies/\"},{\"title\":\"Changes to reviewer volunteering requirement and incentives in May 2025 cycle (EMNLP 2025)\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2025\"},{\"title\":\"Automatically Measuring Peer Review's Utility for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://aclanthology.org/2025.emnlp-main.1476.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Advice on Reviewing for EMNLP\",\"url\":\"https://2020.emnlp.org/blog/2020-05-17-write-good-reviews/\"},{\"title\":\"Review Form\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"[Policy Spotlight] EMNLP 2025 Criteria for “Highly Irresponsible” Reviewers — What It Means & Why It Matters | CSPaper Forum\",\"url\":\"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/70/policy-spotlight-emnlp-2025-criteria-for-highly-irresponsible-reviewers-what-it-means-why-it-matters\"},{\"title\":\"ACL Policies for Review and Citation - Admin Wiki\",\"url\":\"https://www.aclweb.org/adminwiki/index.php/ACL_Policies_for_Review_and_Citation\"},{\"title\":\"Authors Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2025 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP%2F2025%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"‭ACL Peer Review Committee Report‬\",\"url\":\"https://www.aclweb.org/adminwiki/images/d/d3/ACL_Peer_Review_Committee_Report2_Incentives_May_2025.pdf\"}]\n\nI found information about EMNLP 2025 reviewer policies, but the search results don't contain a specific detailed scoring rubric or comprehensive review form guidelines document. Here's what I found:\n\n## Reviewer Guidelines and Policies for EMNLP 2025\n\n**Reviewer Responsibilities and Standards:**\n\nReviews for good-faith work should be substantive, with reviews containing only a single argument (1-2 sentences) and no constructive feedback being flagged as problematic.\n\n**LLM Policy:**\n\nIt is acceptable to use LLMs for paraphrasing, grammatical checks and proof-reading, but not for the content of the (meta-)reviews.\n\n**Author Review Requirements:**\n\nStarting in May 2025, all submitting authors have to also sign up as reviewers (deadline: 48h after the submission deadline).\n\n**Standards for Good-Faith Submissions:**\n\nA good faith article must at minimum state the contribution up front and provide an evaluation that supports that; if the writing is so poor that the intended contribution can't be identified or the article is missing an evaluation, then the article does not warrant a serious review.\n\nThe search results point to the ACL Rolling Review platform (aclrollingreview.org) as the official source for review forms and detailed guidelines. For the most current and specific scoring rubric and review form details, you may want to check the official ARR review form directly at http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"57df35a8-7776-42f2-9a89-3def6408fbf8","uuid":"3132b1cc-7609-46c3-a239-392473d6ce7c","timestamp":"2026-05-14T14:40:28.310Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"EMNLP 2025 review form scoring rubric reviewer guidelines","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_011KhUXrCmt7fJe3ZQL6qrnL","content":[{"title":"Criteria for Determining Irresponsible Reviewers - EMNLP 2025","url":"https://2025.emnlp.org/reviewer-policies/"},{"title":"Changes to reviewer volunteering requirement and incentives in May 2025 cycle (EMNLP 2025)","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2025"},{"title":"Automatically Measuring Peer Review's Utility for Authors","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2025.emnlp-main.1476.pdf"},{"title":"Advice on Reviewing for EMNLP","url":"https://2020.emnlp.org/blog/2020-05-17-write-good-reviews/"},{"title":"Review Form","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform"},{"title":"[Policy Spotlight] EMNLP 2025 Criteria for “Highly Irresponsible” Reviewers — What It Means & Why It Matters | CSPaper Forum","url":"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/70/policy-spotlight-emnlp-2025-criteria-for-highly-irresponsible-reviewers-what-it-means-why-it-matters"},{"title":"ACL Policies for Review and Citation - Admin Wiki","url":"https://www.aclweb.org/adminwiki/index.php/ACL_Policies_for_Review_and_Citation"},{"title":"Authors Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors"},{"title":"EMNLP 2025 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP%2F2025%2FConference"},{"title":"‭ACL Peer Review Committee Report‬","url":"https://www.aclweb.org/adminwiki/images/d/d3/ACL_Peer_Review_Committee_Report2_Incentives_May_2025.pdf"}]},"I found information about EMNLP 2025 reviewer policies, but the search results don't contain a specific detailed scoring rubric or comprehensive review form guidelines document. Here's what I found:\n\n## Reviewer Guidelines and Policies for EMNLP 2025\n\n**Reviewer Responsibilities and Standards:**\n\nReviews for good-faith work should be substantive, with reviews containing only a single argument (1-2 sentences) and no constructive feedback being flagged as problematic.\n\n**LLM Policy:**\n\nIt is acceptable to use LLMs for paraphrasing, grammatical checks and proof-reading, but not for the content of the (meta-)reviews.\n\n**Author Review Requirements:**\n\nStarting in May 2025, all submitting authors have to also sign up as reviewers (deadline: 48h after the submission deadline).\n\n**Standards for Good-Faith Submissions:**\n\nA good faith article must at minimum state the contribution up front and provide an evaluation that supports that; if the writing is so poor that the intended contribution can't be identified or the article is missing an evaluation, then the article does not warrant a serious review.\n\nThe search results point to the ACL Rolling Review platform (aclrollingreview.org) as the official source for review forms and detailed guidelines. For the most current and specific scoring rubric and review form details, you may want to check the official ARR review form directly at http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform."],"durationSeconds":7.925693440999999}}
