{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Gvp65nV2EX5a2cWrWZTr7k","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"ACL Rolling Review review form overall assessment scoring scale 1-5\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Review Form – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"How ARR works – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewing\"},{\"title\":\"ACL 2023 Acceptance Recommendations - ACL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://2023.aclweb.org/blog/overall-recommendation/\"},{\"title\":\"ACL Rolling Review Proposal - Admin Wiki\",\"url\":\"https://www.aclweb.org/adminwiki/index.php?title=ACL_Rolling_Review_Proposal\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Area Chair Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"ACL 2022 Chair Blog Post FAQ\",\"url\":\"https://www.2022.aclweb.org/post/acl-2022-chair-blog-post-faq\"},{\"title\":\"ACL Rolling Review Data Collection (ARR-DC) - ARR Data Collection\",\"url\":\"https://arr-data.aclweb.org/\"},{\"title\":\"Overall score distribution in ARR-3Y and ARR complete reviews. | Download Scientific Diagram\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/figure/Overall-score-distribution-in-ARR-3Y-and-ARR-complete-reviews_fig1_358162807\"},{\"title\":\"Program Chairs’ Report on Peer Review at ACL 2023 Anna Rogers}\",\"url\":\"https://aclanthology.org/2023.acl-long.report.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about the ACL Rolling Review (ARR) overall assessment scoring scale:\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation. The Overall assessment score is an explicit recommendation for the outcome of this paper, if it were committed to an *ACL venue. This is a composite score reflecting your assessment of soundness, excitement, and also other factors like novelty and impact.\n\nFor the meta-review assessment (which is separate from individual reviewer scores), The ARR metareview score has changed in February 2025 to be more aligned with reviewer scores. The new options are: 5 = Consider for Award: I think this paper could be considered for an outstanding paper award at an *ACL conference (up to top 2.5% papers).\n\nThe search results also reference an earlier ARR review scale that used a 1-5 rating system with different descriptors, though the current system emphasizes the three separate scores (soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation) rather than a single overall assessment score on a 1-5 scale.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"57df35a8-7776-42f2-9a89-3def6408fbf8","uuid":"5d88b350-6242-4b7d-985e-1737962c496b","timestamp":"2026-05-14T14:40:38.622Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"ACL Rolling Review review form overall assessment scoring scale 1-5","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01Xp5hxJKZZFMWwd2qf7C7yZ","content":[{"title":"Review Form – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform"},{"title":"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines"},{"title":"How ARR works – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewing"},{"title":"ACL 2023 Acceptance Recommendations - ACL 2023","url":"https://2023.aclweb.org/blog/overall-recommendation/"},{"title":"ACL Rolling Review Proposal - Admin Wiki","url":"https://www.aclweb.org/adminwiki/index.php?title=ACL_Rolling_Review_Proposal"},{"title":"ARR Area Chair Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines"},{"title":"ACL 2022 Chair Blog Post FAQ","url":"https://www.2022.aclweb.org/post/acl-2022-chair-blog-post-faq"},{"title":"ACL Rolling Review Data Collection (ARR-DC) - ARR Data Collection","url":"https://arr-data.aclweb.org/"},{"title":"Overall score distribution in ARR-3Y and ARR complete reviews. | Download Scientific Diagram","url":"https://www.researchgate.net/figure/Overall-score-distribution-in-ARR-3Y-and-ARR-complete-reviews_fig1_358162807"},{"title":"Program Chairs’ Report on Peer Review at ACL 2023 Anna Rogers}","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2023.acl-long.report.pdf"}]},"Based on the search results, here's what I found about the ACL Rolling Review (ARR) overall assessment scoring scale:\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation. The Overall assessment score is an explicit recommendation for the outcome of this paper, if it were committed to an *ACL venue. This is a composite score reflecting your assessment of soundness, excitement, and also other factors like novelty and impact.\n\nFor the meta-review assessment (which is separate from individual reviewer scores), The ARR metareview score has changed in February 2025 to be more aligned with reviewer scores. The new options are: 5 = Consider for Award: I think this paper could be considered for an outstanding paper award at an *ACL conference (up to top 2.5% papers).\n\nThe search results also reference an earlier ARR review scale that used a 1-5 rating system with different descriptors, though the current system emphasizes the three separate scores (soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation) rather than a single overall assessment score on a 1-5 scale."],"durationSeconds":7.270336136000002}}
