{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01J4M75VS4dg5BQCFQjeFwku","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"site:aclrollingreview.org reviewform overall assessment soundness excitement 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Review Form\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Area Chair Guidelines\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Authors Guidelines\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Changelog\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/changelog\"},{\"title\":\"Response to ACL 2023 Questions\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/ACL-2023-session/\"},{\"title\":\"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/\"},{\"title\":\"Incentives 2026\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2026\"},{\"title\":\"Dates and Venues\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/dates\"},{\"title\":\"ARR SAC Guidelines\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/sacguidelines\"}]\n\nI found the search results from the ACL Rolling Review website. Based on the specific query about the review form and the 2025 updates, here are the key findings:\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation.\n\nRegarding the specific scoring categories mentioned in your query:\n\n**Soundness:** The soundness assessment asks whether the paper is sufficiently sound and thorough, whether it clearly states scientific claims and provides adequate support for them, and for experimental papers considers the depth and/or breadth of research questions, technical soundness of experiments, and methodological validity of evaluation. The soundness scores must be justified by the text of the review.\n\n**Excitement:** Excitement is subjective and does not necessarily follow what is popular in the field, and papers may be perceived as transformational/innovative/surprising because they present conceptual breakthroughs or evidence challenging common assumptions/methods/datasets/metrics. Excitement scores reflect reviewers' personal taste, and so do not necessarily come with explicit reasons.\n\n**Overall Assessment:** The Overall assessment score is an explicit recommendation for the outcome of the paper if it were committed to an *ACL venue, and is a composite score reflecting assessment of soundness, excitement, and also other factors like novelty and impact.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"57df35a8-7776-42f2-9a89-3def6408fbf8","uuid":"79a65037-bd38-4624-aef4-ca477d6dcc3f","timestamp":"2026-05-14T14:40:49.486Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"site:aclrollingreview.org reviewform overall assessment soundness excitement 2025","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01XEiwEVMBEVpM8ZpnnicfAo","content":[{"title":"Review Form","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform"},{"title":"ARR Reviewer Guidelines","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines"},{"title":"ARR Area Chair Guidelines","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines"},{"title":"Authors Guidelines","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors"},{"title":"ARR Changelog","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/changelog"},{"title":"Response to ACL 2023 Questions","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/ACL-2023-session/"},{"title":"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/"},{"title":"Incentives 2026","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2026"},{"title":"Dates and Venues","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/dates"},{"title":"ARR SAC Guidelines","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/sacguidelines"}]},"I found the search results from the ACL Rolling Review website. Based on the specific query about the review form and the 2025 updates, here are the key findings:\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation.\n\nRegarding the specific scoring categories mentioned in your query:\n\n**Soundness:** The soundness assessment asks whether the paper is sufficiently sound and thorough, whether it clearly states scientific claims and provides adequate support for them, and for experimental papers considers the depth and/or breadth of research questions, technical soundness of experiments, and methodological validity of evaluation. The soundness scores must be justified by the text of the review.\n\n**Excitement:** Excitement is subjective and does not necessarily follow what is popular in the field, and papers may be perceived as transformational/innovative/surprising because they present conceptual breakthroughs or evidence challenging common assumptions/methods/datasets/metrics. Excitement scores reflect reviewers' personal taste, and so do not necessarily come with explicit reasons.\n\n**Overall Assessment:** The Overall assessment score is an explicit recommendation for the outcome of the paper if it were committed to an *ACL venue, and is a composite score reflecting assessment of soundness, excitement, and also other factors like novelty and impact."],"durationSeconds":6.888414555000003}}
